#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""site — client websites, run from inside a client workspace.

A client site is a public repo under our GitHub org (from one of the
templates in claude-tools/templates/sites/<type>/, cloned into ./repos/<name>) — the repo is the
record and what the client gets on exit — served by **Cloudflare Pages**:
one Pages project per site, created by API, content pushed by direct upload
(`site publish`) after every push. No build, no shared deploy, nothing to
click per client; a custom domain is one API call plus two DNS lines. The
older GitHub Pages path is still here behind `--gh-pages` / for repos made
before 2026-09-16 and goes away once Bleu Grave has moved.

  site new <name> [--template TYPE] [--tagline "…"] [--primary] [--db [--owner EMAIL]] [--no-wait] [--dry-run] [--gh-pages]
  site templates                       # the kinds of site `--template` takes, and what each is
  site checkout <name> --connected [--test] | --key-from NAME [--webhook] [--live] | --off
                                       # Stripe Checkout on a catalog site (SITE_ADMIN=1): --connected = the owner's
                                       # connected account on our platform key (the path, B22); --key-from = their key (fallback)
  site data <name> [--owner EMAIL] [--dry-run]   # give a site its own database + /admin (PLAYBOOK § Data)
  site publish [<name>] [--no-ping] [--dry-run]  # HEAD of ./repos/<name> -> its Pages project (must be committed + pushed)
  site shell [<name>] [--check]        # the /admin shell up to the toolbelt's (B41), commit, push, publish
  site mail [<name>] [--domain D] [--check] [--dry-run]  # the site's address (B75): mailbox + Contact links, published
  site mail platform [--check]         # the Resend domain mail.patchlamp.com + the Porkbun records   (SITE_ADMIN=1)
  site mail doctor                     # the app's mail status, the DNS, this workspace's mailbox vs its links
  site ls                              # repos in ./repos with where they're served
  site domain <name> [example.com]     # custom domain on the project + the DNS lines   (SITE_ADMIN=1)
  site adopt <name> [--project P]      # register an existing repo as a Cloudflare site   (SITE_ADMIN=1)
  site transfer <name> <github-user> [--keep]  # hand the repo to the client             (SITE_ADMIN=1)
  site handover [<name>] [--out DIR] [--no-upload]  # everything that is theirs -> handover/<date>/ + a zip (B69)
  site retire <name> [--delete-repo] [--keep-local]  # take a site down: Pages project + registry row (+ repo)  (SITE_ADMIN=1)
  site stamp <name>                    # (GitHub Pages only) build id into version.json + every page
  site template push [--template T]    # mirror templates/sites/<T> to <org>/site-template(-<T>)
  site watch [--once] [--dry-run] [--rdap] [--site KEY] [--json]   # every live site + preview checked (B72)
  site doctor                          # auth, org, template, Cloudflare, and each repo

Everything but `template` and `doctor` runs only inside a client workspace
(a directory with .client.json; `client new <slug>` makes one) and only
touches ./repos/. Which Pages project a workspace may publish to is
recorded in ~/.config/claude-tools/sites.json by `site new` / `site adopt`
— outside the workspace, so a client session can't point itself at another
client's project. domain, adopt, transfer and retire are Taylor's work: they refuse
unless SITE_ADMIN=1 is in the environment, which a client session can't set.

The data layer (plan 12 § B29): `site data` (or `new --db`) creates one
Cloudflare D1 database named after the Pages project, records its id in the
registry, writes the binding into the repo's wrangler.toml, copies the
Functions shell (functions/: the owner's /admin with a magic-link sign-in,
the /api/* pattern) and migrations/ from templates/sites/_shell, sets the Pages
secrets SESSION_SECRET (random, never printed) and ADMIN_EMAIL, registers the
owner as the project's contact on patchlamp.com (the sign-in link is emailed
through its form endpoint, so the site holds no mail key), applies the
migrations (`db migrate`), commits, pushes and publishes. `site publish`
then deploys functions/ and wrangler.toml beside the static files, which stay
static: Pages runs a Function only for the paths functions/ has. `db` is the
tool for the database itself.

Templates (plan 12 § B30): templates/sites/<type>/ is one kind of site —
business (the default, and what every site before 2026-09-24 came from),
service, portfolio, nonprofit, store, restaurant — each with a
template.json (title, summary, pages, and for a type that needs one
`"db": true` and the collections it starts with). `site new --template
service` makes the database too (as --db) and adds its collections. Each
type's live demo is a client workspace clients/demo-<type> (testaurant for
the restaurant): the demo is that template with demo content, so a demo
that works is a template that works. templates/sites/_shell/ is the data
layer's shared shell (functions/, migrations/), the same for every type.

The badge and the search ping (B60, B49): every template's footer ends with
"Patched by Patchlamp", linking to that segment's page on patchlamp.com with
`?from=badge` so `front` counts what it brings in. A client who would rather
not carry it gets `badge: off` on a line of its own in the workspace's
NOTES.md: the line stays in the repo (the repo is theirs) and `site publish`
leaves it out of the upload. After every publish, `site publish` submits the
site's URLs to IndexNow (Bing, Naver, Seznam, Yandex, Yep — not Google, which
has no such endpoint) on a key of that site's own, kept in the registry and
served from the site as /<key>.txt; `--no-ping` skips it, a ping that fails
never fails the publish, and a site that asks not to be indexed is never
submitted.

The watch (B72, plan ~/projects/plans/30-site-watch.md): `site watch --once`, every 15 minutes from
site-watch.timer, checks every Cloudflare site in the registry and every published preview — DNS (IPv4)
into Cloudflare's ranges, a certificate the system trusts, the home page 200 with a template marker —
and keeps the record in ~/projects/sms-relay/state/uptime.json, which this writes and the relay only
reads (the owner's texts are the relay's `site_down` / `site_back` / `domain_expiry`). Two failed
checks in a row are an outage: `notify` to Taylor with the evidence and one TAYLOR-TODO § 7 entry. A
preview is reported, never texted. Custom domains' expiry by RDAP once a week; inside 30 days, § 7.
uptime.json (version 1; add fields, never rename):
  {version, updated, interval_minutes, last_run: {at, checked, down, took_s, pretend},
   sites: {"<slug>/<repo>" | "preview/<slug>": {kind: client|preview, slug, repo, project, url, host,
     markers, watched_since, first_up, state: up|down|pending|expired|unwatched, fails, fail_since,
     last_check: {at, ok, status, marker, dns, cert_days, ms, problem},
     outage: null | {id, since, confirmed_at, problem},          # set only on the second failed check
     outages: [{id, since, until, minutes, problem}], gaps: [{from, to}],   # 60 days
     domain: {name, host, expires, registrar, days_left, checked_at, error}, filed: {key: at}}}}
A registry row may carry `watch_marker` (the string its home page must hold) or `watch: false`.

Mail (B75, plan ~/projects/plans/34-email.md): every hosted site has an address Patch answers —
<slug>@mail.patchlamp.com, or hello@<domain> for a domain on our Cloudflare account whose apex has no
MX (`--domain`, SITE_ADMIN=1: the Resend domain with receiving on, its records written by the DNS API,
verified, then the mailbox PUT; a domain with mail already refuses — the owner uses the forward). The
mailbox lives on patchlamp.com (GET/PUT /internal/relay/projects/{slug}/mailbox); the site's Contact
block shows it as <a data-mail href="mailto:{{MAIL}}">{{MAIL}}</a>, filled by `site new` and rewritten,
committed, pushed and published by `site mail`. This tool never sends mail; the app does, on the
owner's word, through the relay.

Config, by name, never printed:
  RESEND_API_KEY         `site mail platform` / `--domain` (a full-access key: it makes domains)
  PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET  the mailbox on patchlamp.com (`site mail`, `site new`'s {{MAIL}}, doctor)
  CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN   ~/.config/claude-tools/env — Account: Cloudflare Pages Edit (+ D1 Edit for the data layer)
  CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID  same file. Both required for new/publish/domain.
  GITHUB_TOKEN   passed to gh as GH_TOKEN; when absent, gh's own login is used.
  SITE_ORG       the GitHub owner repos are created under (`setenv.sh SITE_ORG`).
  SITE_TEMPLATE_REPO  name of the mirrored template repo (default site-template).
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import urllib.request
from pathlib import Path
sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "lib"))
import tenant  # noqa: E402  (shared tenant-identity check, B80)

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
SITES_DIR = HERE / "templates" / "sites"
SHELL_DIR = SITES_DIR / "_shell"                  # the data layer's functions/ + migrations/, every type's
DEFAULT_TEMPLATE = "business"
TEMPLATE_DIR = SITES_DIR / DEFAULT_TEMPLATE       # set per call by use_template()
ENV_FILE = Path(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_TOOLS_ENV", Path.home() / ".config/claude-tools/env"))
CLIENT_BIN = HERE / "bin" / "client"
NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,62}$")
DOMAIN_RE = re.compile(r"^(?=.{1,253}$)([a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?\.)+[a-z]{2,}$")
PAGES_IPS = ("185.199.108.153", "185.199.109.153", "185.199.110.153", "185.199.111.153")
FILLED_FILES = ("CLAUDE.md", "README.md", ".claude/settings.json")   # files that carry the live URL
CF_API = os.environ.get("CF_API_BASE") or "https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4"   # env: tests only
STRIPE_API = (os.environ.get("STRIPE_API_BASE") or "https://api.stripe.com").rstrip("/")   # env: tests only
REGISTRY = ENV_FILE.parent / "sites.json"          # slug -> repo -> {host, project, domains}; not in any workspace
WRANGLER = HERE / "node_modules" / ".bin" / "wrangler"
NON_SITE = {"CLAUDE.md", "README.md", ".claude", "tools", ".gitignore", ".nojekyll",
            "CNAME", ".github", "version.json", "shots",
            "functions", "migrations", "wrangler.toml", ".dev.vars", ".wrangler", "seed.sql"}   # in the repo, not on the site
DATA_PARTS = ("functions", "migrations")          # in templates/sites/_shell, copied only for a site with a database
TEMPLATE_META = "template.json"                   # in each type's folder; about the template, never copied
LIBRARY = "sections"                              # a type's section library (leads preview --from renders it); never copied
DB_BIN = HERE / "bin" / "db"
NEWSLETTER_BIN = HERE / "bin" / "newsletter"
COMPAT_DATE = "2026-09-01"                        # Workers runtime date for the site's Functions
PREVIEWS_PROJECT = "patchlamp-previews"           # B45: the one project every lead preview lives in
DRY = False
CREATED = set()                                   # Pages projects made in this run


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers

def die(msg, code=1):
    print(f"site: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


def say(msg=""):
    print(msg, flush=True)


def read_env():
    """Parse the toolbelt env file. Values stay in memory only."""
    keys = {}
    if not ENV_FILE.exists():
        return keys
    for line in ENV_FILE.read_text().splitlines():
        if not line or line.startswith("#") or "=" not in line:
            continue
        k, v = line.split("=", 1)
        keys[k.strip()] = v.strip()
    return keys


def token_source():
    """('GITHUB_TOKEN', value) from the toolbelt, else ('gh login', None)."""
    val = os.environ.get("GH_TOKEN") or os.environ.get("GITHUB_TOKEN")
    if val:
        return "GH_TOKEN from the environment", val
    val = read_env().get("GITHUB_TOKEN")
    if val:
        return "GITHUB_TOKEN from the toolbelt", val
    return "gh's own login (no GITHUB_TOKEN in the toolbelt)", None


def gh_env():
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env["GH_PROMPT_DISABLED"] = "1"
    env["GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT"] = "0"
    env["GH_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER"] = "1"
    _, tok = token_source()
    if tok:
        env["GH_TOKEN"] = tok
    return env


def gh(*args, check=True, stdin=None, quiet=False):
    """Run gh; returns (returncode, stdout, stderr). Never echoes the token."""
    cmd = ["gh", *args]
    if DRY:
        say("  would run: " + " ".join(cmd))
        return 0, "", ""
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, env=gh_env(), input=stdin)
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        if not quiet:
            die(f"gh {' '.join(args[:3])} failed: {r.stderr.strip() or r.stdout.strip()}")
    return r.returncode, r.stdout.strip(), r.stderr.strip()


def gh_json(*args, default=None):
    code, out, _ = gh(*args, check=False)
    if code != 0 or not out:
        return default
    try:
        return json.loads(out)
    except ValueError:
        return default


def git(repo, *args, check=True):
    cmd = ["git", "-C", str(repo), *args]
    if DRY:
        say("  would run: " + " ".join(cmd))
        return 0, ""
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, env=gh_env())
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        die(f"git {' '.join(args[:2])} failed in {repo}: {r.stderr.strip() or r.stdout.strip()}")
    return r.returncode, r.stdout.strip()


def owner():
    o = os.environ.get("SITE_ORG") or read_env().get("SITE_ORG")
    if not o:
        die("SITE_ORG is not set: the GitHub org (or user) repos are created under. "
            "Taylor sets it once with ~/.config/claude-tools/setenv.sh SITE_ORG "
            "(the org is TAYLOR-TODO §1); for a dry run, SITE_ORG=Taylor-Rem site …")
    if not re.match(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]{0,38}$", o):
        die(f"SITE_ORG {o!r} is not a valid GitHub owner name")
    return o


def template_repo():
    return os.environ.get("SITE_TEMPLATE_REPO", "site-template")


def workspace():
    """The client workspace is the cwd: must hold .client.json."""
    ws = Path.cwd()
    p = ws / ".client.json"
    if not p.exists():
        die("not in a client workspace (no .client.json here). Run this from "
            "~/projects/clients/<slug>; `client new <slug> --name …` makes one.")
    try:
        meta = json.loads(p.read_text())
    except ValueError as exc:
        die(f".client.json is not valid JSON: {exc}")
    if not meta.get("slug"):
        die(".client.json has no slug; run client new <slug> --restamp")
    tenant.enforce(meta["slug"], die)
    return ws, meta


# Server-side pieces of a Cloudflare Pages deploy. A demo in "static" mode may
# publish page edits but not changes to these — a stranger steering a demo mustn't
# push live Functions/headers/redirects (sandbox-F3).
DEMO_SERVER_PATHS = ("functions", "_worker.js", "_routes.json", "_headers",
                     "_redirects", "wrangler.toml", "wrangler.jsonc", "wrangler.json")


def demo_publish_block(meta, d):
    """None if this demo may publish; else the reason it may not. `demo reset`
    sets SITE_DEMO_RESET to bypass this — the nightly reset always republishes."""
    mode = meta.get("demo_publish", "static")
    if mode == "off":
        return ("this is a demo site, so changes go live only on its nightly reset. Your edit is "
                "saved in the repo; the reset is what puts it on the web.")
    has_golden = git(d, "rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", "golden^{commit}", check=False)[0] == 0
    if has_golden:
        changed = git(d, "diff", "--name-only", "golden", "HEAD", check=False)[1].splitlines()
    else:
        changed = git(d, "ls-files", check=False)[1].splitlines()
    hits = sorted({c for c in changed if any(c == p or c.startswith(p + "/") for p in DEMO_SERVER_PATHS)})
    if hits:
        return ("this demo can put page edits live, but not changes to how its site runs "
                f"({', '.join(hits[:6])}). Those stay until the nightly reset.")
    return None


def repos_of(ws):
    d = ws / "repos"
    return sorted(r.name for r in d.iterdir() if (r / ".git").exists()) if d.is_dir() else []


def repo_dir(ws, name):
    if not NAME_RE.match(name):
        die(f"{name!r} is not a valid site name (lowercase letters, digits, dashes)")
    d = ws / "repos" / name
    if not (d / ".git").exists():
        die(f"no repo at repos/{name} (site ls shows what exists)")
    return d


def remote_slug(repo):
    """'owner/name' from the origin remote, or None."""
    code, url = git(repo, "remote", "get-url", "origin", check=False)
    if code != 0:
        return None
    m = re.search(r"github\.com[:/]([^/]+)/([^/.]+?)(?:\.git)?/?$", url)
    return f"{m.group(1)}/{m.group(2)}" if m else None


def pages_info(slug):
    """The Pages object for owner/name, or None (not enabled / no access)."""
    return gh_json("api", f"repos/{slug}/pages")


def pages_url(o, name):
    return f"https://{o.lower()}.github.io/{name}/"


def require_admin(what):
    if os.environ.get("SITE_ADMIN") != "1":
        die(f"{what} is Taylor's work (an account or DNS change). Run it as "
            f"`SITE_ADMIN=1 site {what} …` from an owner session; a client session "
            f"can't. Reply to the client that this needs Taylor and FORWARD-TO-TAYLOR it.")


def write_meta(ws, meta):
    (ws / ".client.json").write_text(json.dumps(meta, indent=2) + "\n")


def restamp(ws, meta):
    """Re-run `client new <slug> --restamp` so CLAUDE.md and the allowlist follow
    .client.json (the curl rules for live_url live there)."""
    client = CLIENT_BIN if CLIENT_BIN.exists() else shutil.which("client")
    if not client:
        say("  note: `client` not found; run `client new "
            f"{meta['slug']} --restamp` yourself so the allowlist gains the curl rules")
        return
    cmd = [str(client), "new", meta["slug"], "--restamp"]
    if DRY:
        say("  would run: " + " ".join(cmd))
        return
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env.setdefault("CLIENTS_DIR", str(ws.parent))
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        say(f"  WARN restamp failed: {r.stderr.strip() or r.stdout.strip()}")
    else:
        say(f"  restamped workspace (CLAUDE.md + allowlist now know {meta.get('live_url') or 'no live URL'})")


def set_live_url(ws, meta, url, force=False):
    """live_url is the one URL the allowlist lets a session curl. Take it when
    it's empty; otherwise only with --primary."""
    cur = meta.get("live_url") or ""
    if cur and not force and cur != url:
        say(f"  live_url stays {cur} (use --primary to make {url} the one the "
            f"allowlist can curl; multi-site allowlists are a `client` follow-up)")
        return False
    meta["live_url"] = url
    if not DRY:
        write_meta(ws, meta)
    say(f"  .client.json live_url = {url}")
    return True


def fill(text, values):
    for k, v in values.items():
        text = text.replace("{{" + k + "}}", v)
    return text


def http_status(url, timeout=10):
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, method="GET", headers={"User-Agent": "claude-tools site", "Cache-Control": "no-cache"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:
            return r.status, r.read(4096).decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        return exc.code, ""
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError):
        return 0, ""


def wait_live(url, marker, seconds=240):
    """Poll until the live URL serves `marker` (or `seconds` pass)."""
    say(f"  waiting for Pages to publish {url} (up to {seconds // 60} min; --no-wait skips)")
    deadline = time.time() + seconds
    while time.time() < deadline:
        code, body = http_status(url)
        if code == 200 and (not marker or marker in body):
            return True
        time.sleep(10)
    return False


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cloudflare

def cf_creds(required=True):
    """(token, account_id) from the toolbelt. Values stay in memory."""
    env = read_env()
    tok = os.environ.get("CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN") or env.get("CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN")
    acct = os.environ.get("CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID") or env.get("CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID")
    if required and not (tok and acct):
        die("CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID are needed in the toolbelt "
            "(~/.config/claude-tools/setenv.sh <NAME>; TAYLOR-TODO §1 hosting step 0)")
    return tok, acct


def cf_api(method, path, body=None, ok404=False):
    """One Cloudflare API call. Returns the `result`; dies on an error unless
    ok404 and the thing isn't there (then None)."""
    tok, acct = cf_creds()
    url = f"{CF_API}/accounts/{acct}{path}"
    if DRY and method != "GET":
        say(f"  would {method} {path}" + (f" {json.dumps(body)}" if body else ""))
        return {}
    data = json.dumps(body).encode() if body is not None else None
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, method=method,
                                 headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {tok}", "Content-Type": "application/json",
                                          "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            payload = json.loads(r.read().decode())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        if exc.code == 404 and ok404:
            return None
        try:
            errs = json.loads(exc.read().decode()).get("errors", [])
            msg = "; ".join(f"{e.get('code')}: {e.get('message')}" for e in errs) or f"HTTP {exc.code}"
        except ValueError:
            msg = f"HTTP {exc.code}"
        die(f"Cloudflare {method} {path}: {msg}")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
        die(f"Cloudflare {method} {path}: {exc}")
    if not payload.get("success"):
        die(f"Cloudflare {method} {path}: {payload.get('errors')}")
    return payload.get("result")


def cf_project(name):
    return cf_api("GET", f"/pages/projects/{name}", ok404=True)


def cf_ensure_project(name):
    """The Pages project for a site, created on first use. Production branch
    `main`, no source (direct upload)."""
    for i in range(6 if name in CREATED else 1):     # just made: the API can take a few seconds to show it
        p = cf_project(name)
        if p:
            return p
        if name in CREATED:
            time.sleep(3)
    if name in CREATED:
        return {"name": name, "subdomain": f"{name}.pages.dev"}
    p = cf_api("POST", "/pages/projects", {"name": name, "production_branch": "main"})
    CREATED.add(name)
    if (p or {}).get("subdomain"):
        HOSTS[name] = p["subdomain"]
    say(f"  created Pages project {name} -> https://{(p or {}).get('subdomain') or name + '.pages.dev'}")
    return p or {"name": name, "subdomain": f"{name}.pages.dev"}


HOSTS = {}


def pages_host(project):
    """The project's real *.pages.dev host. Pages subdomains are global: when
    `<name>.pages.dev` is someone else's, Cloudflare gives ours a suffix
    (demo-business-ctm.pages.dev), so never build the host from the name."""
    if project not in HOSTS:
        for rows in registry_load().values():
            for r in rows.values():
                if r.get("project") == project and r.get("pages_host"):
                    HOSTS[project] = r["pages_host"]
    if project not in HOSTS:
        p = cf_project(project) if not DRY and cf_creds(required=False)[0] else None
        HOSTS[project] = (p or {}).get("subdomain") or f"{project}.pages.dev"
    return HOSTS[project]


def cf_domains(project):
    return cf_api("GET", f"/pages/projects/{project}/domains") or []


def registry_load():
    if not REGISTRY.exists():
        return {}
    try:
        return json.loads(REGISTRY.read_text())
    except ValueError:
        die(f"{REGISTRY} is not valid JSON")


def registry_save(reg):
    REGISTRY.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = REGISTRY.with_suffix(".json.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(reg, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
    tmp.replace(REGISTRY)


def site_entry(meta, name):
    """The registry row for this workspace's repo, or None (= GitHub Pages / unknown)."""
    return registry_load().get(meta["slug"], {}).get(name)


def templates():
    """{type: template.json} for every kind of site in templates/sites/."""
    out = {}
    for d in sorted(SITES_DIR.iterdir()) if SITES_DIR.is_dir() else []:
        if d.is_dir() and not d.name.startswith("_") and (d / "index.html").exists():
            try:
                info = json.loads((d / TEMPLATE_META).read_text()) if (d / TEMPLATE_META).exists() else {}
            except ValueError:
                info = {"summary": f"({TEMPLATE_META} doesn't parse)"}
            out[d.name] = info
    return out


def use_template(kind):
    """Point TEMPLATE_DIR at templates/sites/<kind>; its template.json."""
    global TEMPLATE_DIR
    kind = kind or DEFAULT_TEMPLATE
    have = templates()
    if kind not in have:
        die(f"no template {kind!r}: {', '.join(have) or 'none found'} (site templates)")
    TEMPLATE_DIR = SITES_DIR / kind
    return have[kind]


def cmd_templates(a):
    for kind, info in templates().items():
        extra = f" — database: {', '.join(info.get('collections') or [])}" if info.get("db") else ""
        say(f"{kind:<11} {info.get('summary', '')}{extra}")
        demo = info.get("demo")
        if demo:
            say(f"{'':<11} demo: {demo}")


def site_register(meta, name, project, domains=None, template=None):
    reg = registry_load()
    row = reg.setdefault(meta["slug"], {}).setdefault(name, {})
    row.update({"host": "cloudflare", "project": project})
    if not DRY and pages_host(project) != f"{project}.pages.dev":
        row["pages_host"] = pages_host(project)        # a suffixed host (the name was taken on pages.dev)
    if template:
        row["template"] = template
    if domains is not None:
        row["domains"] = domains
    if not DRY:
        registry_save(reg)
    return row


def wrangler(*args, env_extra=None, cwd=None):
    """Run wrangler from claude-tools' node_modules with the Cloudflare creds in
    its environment (never on the command line). Returns (code, output)."""
    if not WRANGLER.exists():
        die(f"wrangler is not installed at {WRANGLER}; run claude-tools/install.sh (npm install)")
    tok, acct = cf_creds()
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env.update({"CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN": tok, "CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID": acct,
                "WRANGLER_SEND_METRICS": "false", "CI": "1", "NO_COLOR": "1"})
    env.update(env_extra or {})
    cmd = [str(WRANGLER), *args]
    if DRY:
        say("  would run: wrangler " + " ".join(args))
        return 0, ""
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, env=env, cwd=str(cwd or HERE))
    return r.returncode, (r.stdout + "\n" + r.stderr).strip()


def export_tree(repo, dest, server=None):
    """The committed tree of HEAD, minus the files that are about the repo
    rather than on the site. The working copy is never published: what's
    served is exactly what's in git. With `server` (a directory), a site with
    a database is laid out the way `wrangler pages deploy` wants it:
    server/functions/ and server/wrangler.toml beside dest (the static files),
    and never inside it — the Functions' source and the migrations are not
    pages."""
    archive = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(repo), "archive", "--format=tar", "HEAD"],
                             capture_output=True)
    if archive.returncode != 0:
        die(f"git archive failed: {archive.stderr.decode().strip()}")
    subprocess.run(["tar", "-x", "-C", str(dest)], input=archive.stdout, check=True)
    if server is not None and (dest / "functions").is_dir():
        shutil.move(str(dest / "functions"), str(server / "functions"))
        toml = (dest / "wrangler.toml").read_text() if (dest / "wrangler.toml").exists() else ""
        rel = os.path.relpath(dest, server)
        toml = re.sub(r'(?m)^pages_build_output_dir\s*=.*$', f'pages_build_output_dir = "{rel}"', toml)
        if "pages_build_output_dir" not in toml:
            toml = f'pages_build_output_dir = "{rel}"\n' + toml
        (server / "wrangler.toml").write_text(toml)
    for name in NON_SITE:
        p = dest / name
        if p.is_dir():
            shutil.rmtree(p)
        elif p.exists():
            p.unlink()
    n = sum(1 for p in dest.rglob("*") if p.is_file())
    if not (dest / "index.html").exists():
        die("the repo has no index.html at its root; nothing to publish")
    if not (dest / "404.html").exists():
        say("  WARN no 404.html: Pages will answer every missing path with index.html (200); copy the template's")
    return n


def curl_header(url, name):
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, method="HEAD", headers={"User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:
            return r.headers.get(name)
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError):
        return None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the badge (B60)
#
# Every template's footer ends with one line: "Patched by Patchlamp", linking to
# that segment's page on patchlamp.com with ?from=badge so `front` counts it
# (GROWTH § 15.2, § 18; BRAND.md promises it). A client who would rather not
# carry it writes `badge: off` on a line of its own in the workspace's NOTES.md:
# the line stays in the repo — the repo is the client's record and a restamp
# never rewrites a page — and `site publish` leaves it out of what it uploads.

# the badge is one line of one element: <p> in every template, a <span> or <div>
# where a hand-built footer reads better that way
BADGE_LINE = re.compile(r'(?m)^[ \t]*<(p|span|div|li)\b[^>]*class="patchlamp-badge".*?</\1>[ \t]*\r?\n')
BADGE_OFF = re.compile(r"(?mi)^\s*(?:[-*]\s+)?(?:\*\*)?badge(?:\*\*)?:\s*off\b")


def badge_off(ws):
    """True when this workspace's NOTES.md says `badge: off` (PLAYBOOK § The badge)."""
    try:
        return bool(BADGE_OFF.search((ws / "NOTES.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8")))
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
        return False


def strip_badge(dest):
    """Take the badge out of every page of an export tree; how many pages changed."""
    n = 0
    for p in sorted(dest.rglob("*.html")):
        try:
            text = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            continue
        out = BADGE_LINE.sub("", text)
        if out != text:
            p.write_text(out, encoding="utf-8")
            n += 1
    return n


def has_badge(d):
    """True when the repo's home page carries the badge."""
    p = d / "index.html"
    try:
        return bool(BADGE_LINE.search(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")))
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
        return False


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- IndexNow (B49)
#
# A publish tells IndexNow what changed, so Bing, Naver, Seznam, Yandex and Yep
# re-crawl in minutes instead of weeks. Google has no such endpoint: it finds
# the pages through Search Console (TODO §1), which is why this is only half of
# B49. patchlamp.com does the same from its own deploy (`indexnow:ping`), on one
# key in its config; a client site is not ours, so each gets a key of its own,
# kept in the registry and served from the site as /<key>.txt — that file is how
# IndexNow checks the host belongs to whoever submitted it. A ping never fails a
# publish: the site is already live by the time it runs.

INDEXNOW_ENDPOINT = os.environ.get("INDEXNOW_ENDPOINT") or "https://api.indexnow.org/indexnow"
INDEXNOW_KEY_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9-]{8,128}$")


def registry_set(meta, name, **fields):
    """Add or update fields on this workspace's registry row (never renames one)."""
    reg = registry_load()
    row = reg.setdefault(meta["slug"], {}).setdefault(name, {})
    row.update(fields)
    if not DRY:
        registry_save(reg)
    return row


def site_host(entry, project):
    """The host to submit: the custom domain if there is one, else the Pages host."""
    for dom in entry.get("domains") or []:
        if not dom.startswith("www."):
            return dom
    return entry.get("pages_host") or pages_host(project)


def site_urls(d, base):
    """What to submit: the sitemap's URLs if the repo has one, else the home page
    and every other top-level page in it. IndexNow takes 10,000 at most."""
    sm = d / "sitemap.xml"
    if sm.exists():
        try:
            locs = [u.strip() for u in re.findall(r"<loc>([^<]+)</loc>", sm.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))]
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            locs = []
        if locs:
            return locs[:10000]
    urls = [base]
    for p in sorted(d.glob("*.html")):
        if p.name in ("index.html", "404.html") or p.name in NON_SITE:
            continue
        urls.append(base + p.name)
    return urls[:10000]


def indexnow_key(d, meta, name, entry):
    """This site's key, made once, in the registry and served from the repo as
    /<key>.txt. Returns the key, or None when the file can't be committed and
    pushed — an unreachable key file is a 403 from IndexNow, so we don't ping."""
    key = entry.get("indexnow_key")
    if not (key and INDEXNOW_KEY_RE.match(key)):
        key = secrets.token_hex(16)
        registry_set(meta, name, indexnow_key=key)
        say(f"  IndexNow: new key for this site, in {REGISTRY.name} (never printed)")
    f = d / f"{key}.txt"
    if f.exists() and f.read_text(encoding="utf-8").strip() == key:
        return key
    f.write_text(key + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    git(d, "add", "--", f.name, check=False)
    code, out = git(d, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
                    "commit", "-q", "-m", "IndexNow key file (site publish submits this site's URLs)",
                    "--", f.name, check=False)
    if code != 0:
        # leave nothing uncommitted behind: the next publish refuses a dirty tree
        git(d, "restore", "--staged", "--", f.name, check=False)
        f.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        say(f"  note: IndexNow key file not committed ({out.splitlines()[-1] if out else 'git commit failed'}); no ping")
        return None
    code, out = git(d, "push", "-q", check=False)
    if code != 0:
        say(f"  note: IndexNow key file committed but not pushed ({out.splitlines()[-1] if out else 'git push failed'})")
    say("  IndexNow: key file added to the repo (one text file at the site root)")
    return key


def indexnow_post(host, key, urls):
    """(status, note): the POST IndexNow wants. 200/202 is accepted."""
    body = json.dumps({"host": host, "key": key, "keyLocation": f"https://{host}/{key}.txt",
                       "urlList": urls}).encode()
    req = urllib.request.Request(INDEXNOW_ENDPOINT, data=body, method="POST",
                                 headers={"Content-Type": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
                                          "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:
            return r.status, ""
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        return exc.code, {403: f"the key file at /{key}.txt was not reachable",
                          422: "IndexNow says the host and the URLs disagree"}.get(exc.code, "")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
        return 0, str(exc)


def indexnow_key_for(ws, meta, name, d, entry, project):
    """Before the upload: this site's key in the registry and its key file in the
    repo, or None when there is nothing to submit. Never raises."""
    try:
        robots = (d / "robots.txt")
        noindex = robots.exists() and "noindex" in robots.read_text(encoding="utf-8").lower()
        if project == PREVIEWS_PROJECT or noindex:
            say("  IndexNow: skipped (this site asks not to be indexed)")
            return None
        return indexnow_key(d, meta, name, entry)
    except Exception as exc:                                  # noqa: BLE001 - a search ping never breaks a deploy
        say(f"  IndexNow: skipped ({type(exc).__name__}: {exc})")
        return None


def indexnow_submit(meta, name, d, entry, project, key):
    """After the upload: submit this site's URLs. Says one line and returns; never
    raises, never fails the publish."""
    try:
        host = site_host(entry, project)
        urls = site_urls(d, f"https://{host}/")
        status, note = indexnow_post(host, key, urls)
        ok = status in (200, 202)
        registry_set(meta, name, indexnow={"at": datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
                                           "host": host, "urls": len(urls), "status": status, "ok": ok})
        say(f"  IndexNow: {len(urls)} URL(s) -> {host} "
            + (f"accepted ({status})" if ok else f"not accepted ({status or 'no answer'})"
               + (f": {note}" if note else "") + " — the publish stands"))
    except Exception as exc:                                  # noqa: BLE001 - a search ping never breaks a deploy
        say(f"  IndexNow: skipped ({type(exc).__name__}: {exc})")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- commands

def cmd_new(a):
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    ws, meta = workspace()
    name = a.name
    if not NAME_RE.match(name):
        die(f"{name!r} is not a valid site name: lowercase letters, digits and dashes, "
            f"e.g. {meta['slug']}-site")
    o = owner()
    slug = f"{o}/{name}"
    dest = ws / "repos" / name
    if dest.exists():
        die(f"repos/{name} already exists")
    kind = a.template or meta.get("template") or DEFAULT_TEMPLATE
    tinfo = use_template(kind)
    if tinfo.get("db") and not a.db:
        if a.gh_pages:
            die(f"the {kind} template needs a database, which needs a Cloudflare site; drop --gh-pages")
        a.db = True
        say(f"  the {kind} template keeps {', '.join(tinfo.get('collections') or [])} in a database of the site's own: --db")
    src, _ = token_source()
    say(f"site new {name} for {meta['name']} ({meta['slug']}) under {o}, template {kind}, auth: {src}")

    code, _, err = gh("repo", "view", slug, "--json", "name", check=False)
    if code == 0 and not DRY:
        die(f"{slug} already exists on GitHub; pick another name or clone it into repos/{name}")
    # Plan 02: the plan covers N sites (.client.json "sites", from the tier via
    # `client new --sites`). Counted here, outside the client's write scope, so
    # Patch explains the plan instead of routing around it. SITE_ADMIN=1 overrides.
    allowed = meta.get("sites")
    allowed = 1 if allowed is None else int(allowed)
    have = sorted(set(registry_load().get(meta["slug"], {})) | set(p.name for p in (ws / "repos").iterdir() if (p / ".git").exists())) \
        if (ws / "repos").is_dir() else sorted(registry_load().get(meta["slug"], {}))
    if len(have) >= allowed and os.environ.get("SITE_ADMIN") != "1":
        die(f"this plan covers {allowed} site{'s' if allowed != 1 else ''} and {meta['name']} already has "
            f"{len(have)} ({', '.join(have)}). A second site is a second plan on Starter, or an add-on on "
            f"Standard and up — tell the client plainly and FORWARD-TO-TAYLOR it (PLAYBOOK.md 'A second "
            f"website'). Taylor: SITE_ADMIN=1 site new {name}, or client new {meta['slug']} --restamp --sites N.")
    cloudflare = not a.gh_pages
    if a.db and not cloudflare:
        die("--db needs a Cloudflare site (the database is bound to the Pages project); drop --gh-pages")
    if a.db and not DRY:
        d1_check()                                   # the token must manage D1 before anything is made
        data_owner(ws, meta, a.owner)
    if cloudflare:
        cf_creds()                                   # fail before creating anything
        if cf_project(name):
            die(f"a Pages project named {name} already exists on Cloudflare; pick another name")
        for s_, repos in registry_load().items():
            if name in repos:
                die(f"{name} is already registered to workspace {s_}")
    if cloudflare and not DRY:
        cf_ensure_project(name)                      # first: the URL filled into the files is its real host
    url = f"https://{pages_host(name)}/" if cloudflare else pages_url(o, name)
    values = {
        "NAME": meta["name"], "REPO": name, "URL": url, "OWNER": o,
        "YEAR": str(datetime.date.today().year),
        "TAGLINE": a.tagline or f"A short line about what {meta['name']} does.",
    }
    mail = mail_for_new_site(meta["slug"])            # B75: the Contact block's address ('' = leave the line out)
    if DRY:
        say(f"  would create public repo {slug} from {TEMPLATE_DIR} (template {kind})")
        say(f"  would clone it to repos/{name}, fill {', '.join(f'{{{{{k}}}}}' for k in values)}, "
            f"{{{{MAIL}}}} = {mail or '(none: the Contact line is left out)'}")
        if cloudflare:
            say(f"  would create Cloudflare Pages project {name}, register it, publish, and expect {url}")
        if a.db:
            say(f"  would give it a database: site data {name}" + (f" --owner {a.owner}" if a.owner else ""))
            for c in tinfo.get("collections") or []:
                say(f"  would add the {c} collection: db add {c}")
        else:
            say(f"  would enable GitHub Pages from main:/ and expect {url}")
        set_live_url(ws, meta, url, a.primary)
        restamp(ws, meta)
        say("dry run: nothing created")
        return

    # 1. the repo
    desc = f"Website for {meta['name']}"
    gh("repo", "create", slug, "--public", "--description", desc, "--disable-wiki")
    say(f"  created https://github.com/{slug}")

    # 2. the files, from the local template, placeholders filled before the first commit
    (ws / "repos").mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    shutil.copytree(TEMPLATE_DIR, dest, symlinks=False,
                    ignore=lambda d, names: [n for n in names if Path(d) == TEMPLATE_DIR and n in DATA_PARTS + (TEMPLATE_META, LIBRARY)])
    unfilled = []
    for p in dest.rglob("*"):
        if not p.is_file() or ".git" in p.parts[len(dest.parts):][:1]:
            continue
        try:
            text = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        except (UnicodeDecodeError, OSError):
            continue
        if "{{" in text:
            text = fill_mail(fill(text, values), mail)
            p.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")
            if "{{" in text:
                unfilled.append(str(p.relative_to(dest)))
    if unfilled:
        say(f"  WARN unfilled placeholders in: {', '.join(unfilled)}")

    # 3. push
    git(dest, "init", "-q", "-b", "main")
    git(dest, "add", "-A")
    git(dest, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
        "commit", "-q", "-m", f"New site for {meta['name']} from the {kind} template")
    git(dest, "remote", "add", "origin", f"git@github.com:{slug}.git")
    git(dest, "push", "-q", "-u", "origin", "main")
    say(f"  pushed repos/{name} (main)")

    # 4. the host
    if cloudflare:
        cf_ensure_project(name)
        site_register(meta, name, name, template=kind)
        say(f"  registered {meta['slug']}/{name} -> Pages project {name}")
    else:
        code, out, err = gh("api", "-X", "POST", f"repos/{slug}/pages", "--input", "-",
                            stdin=json.dumps({"source": {"branch": "main", "path": "/"}}), check=False)
        if code != 0 and "already" not in (out + err).lower():
            say(f"  WARN could not enable Pages: {err or out}. Enable it in the repo's Settings → Pages "
                f"(main, root) or run: gh api -X POST repos/{slug}/pages --input - <<< "
                f"'{{\"source\":{{\"branch\":\"main\",\"path\":\"/\"}}}}'")
        info = pages_info(slug) or {}
        if info.get("html_url") and info["html_url"].rstrip("/") + "/" != url:
            say(f"  WARN Pages reports {info['html_url']}, files were filled with {url}")
            url = info["html_url"].rstrip("/") + "/"
        say(f"  GitHub Pages on: {url}")

    # 5. the workspace
    set_live_url(ws, meta, url, a.primary)
    restamp(ws, meta)

    # 6. the data layer, then publish / is it up?
    if a.db:
        enable_data(ws, name, a.owner)
        for c in tinfo.get("collections") or []:
            r = subprocess.run([str(DB_BIN), "add", c, "--site", name], capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=str(ws))
            say(f"  db add {c}: " + ("ok" if r.returncode == 0 else f"FAILED {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[:200]}"))
        git(dest, "add", "-A", "functions", "migrations")
        _, staged = git(dest, "diff", "--cached", "--name-only", check=False)
        if staged.strip():
            git(dest, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
                "commit", "-q", "-m", f"The {kind} template's lists: {', '.join(tinfo.get('collections') or [])}")
            git(dest, "push", "-q")
    if cloudflare:
        cmd_publish(argparse.Namespace(name=name, dry_run=False))
        live = True
    else:
        live = wait_live(url, meta["name"]) if not a.no_wait else False
    say()
    say(f"repo:  https://github.com/{slug}")
    say(f"local: repos/{name}  (git -C repos/{name} …; its CLAUDE.md is the site manual)")
    say(f"live:  {url}  {'— serving' if live else '— not serving yet; Pages usually takes 1–3 minutes'}")
    say(f"next:  edit the REPLACE-ME placeholders in repos/{name}/index.html, commit, push"
        + (f", site publish {name}" if cloudflare else "") + f", then shot {url}")
    if meta.get("live_url") == url:
        say(f"       config.json (if the project entry lists live_url): client snippet {meta['slug']}")


def cmd_publish(a):
    """HEAD of ./repos/<name> -> its Cloudflare Pages project, by direct upload.
    The repo must be committed and pushed: the repo is the record, Pages is a
    mirror of it, and a client session's `git push` is what makes the change
    theirs. Which project is this repo's comes from the registry, never from
    an argument."""
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    ws, meta = workspace()
    names = repos_of(ws)
    name = a.name or (names[0] if len(names) == 1 else None)
    if not name:
        die("which site? site publish <name> (site ls shows them)")
    d = repo_dir(ws, name)
    entry = site_entry(meta, name)
    if not entry or entry.get("host") != "cloudflare":
        die(f"repos/{name} isn't a Cloudflare site in the registry. GitHub Pages repos deploy on push "
            f"(nothing to run); to move one: SITE_ADMIN=1 site adopt {name} from an owner session.")
    project = entry["project"]

    if is_demo(meta.get("slug", "")) and not os.environ.get("SITE_DEMO_RESET"):
        blocked = demo_publish_block(meta, d)
        if blocked:
            die(blocked)

    _, dirty = git(d, "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=no", check=False)
    if dirty.strip():
        die(f"repos/{name} has uncommitted changes; commit (and push) first — what's published is HEAD")
    _, branch = git(d, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "HEAD", check=False)
    if branch != "main" and not DRY:                 # a dry run reads nothing from git, so it has no branch
        die(f"repos/{name} is on {branch!r}; publish from main")
    _, unpushed = git(d, "log", "--oneline", "@{u}..", check=False)
    if unpushed.strip():
        die(f"repos/{name} has unpushed commits; git -C repos/{name} push first, then publish")
    no_ping = getattr(a, "no_ping", False)
    key = None if (no_ping or DRY) else indexnow_key_for(ws, meta, name, d, entry, project)
    _, sha = git(d, "rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD", check=False)
    _, subject = git(d, "log", "-1", "--format=%s", check=False)
    server = (d / "functions").is_dir()
    if server:
        problem = binding_problem(d, entry)
        if problem:
            die(f"repos/{name} has functions/ but {problem}. `site data {name}` sets the database up; "
                f"`client doctor` / `db doctor` say what's off.")

    cf_ensure_project(project)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=f"site-publish-{name}-") as tmp:
        root = Path(tmp)
        out = root / "public"
        out.mkdir()
        n = export_tree(d, out, server=root if server else None)
        if badge_off(ws):
            cut = strip_badge(out)
            say(f"  badge: off in NOTES.md — \"Patched by Patchlamp\" left out of {cut} page(s) "
                f"(the line stays in the repo)")
        say(f"publishing repos/{name} @ {sha} ({n} files{', with its Functions and database binding' if server else ''}) -> {project}")
        code, log = wrangler("pages", "deploy", str(out), "--project-name", project, "--branch", "main",
                             "--commit-hash", sha, "--commit-message", subject[:200], "--commit-dirty=false",
                             cwd=root)
    if DRY:
        say("dry run: nothing published")
        if not no_ping:
            say(f"  would submit this site's URLs to IndexNow ({INDEXNOW_ENDPOINT}); --no-ping skips it")
        return
    if code != 0:
        tail = "\n".join(log.splitlines()[-8:])
        die(f"wrangler pages deploy failed:\n{tail}")
    m = re.search(r"https://[a-z0-9.-]+\.pages\.dev", log)
    preview = m.group(0) if m else None
    prod = f"https://{pages_host(project)}/"
    live = None
    for dom in entry.get("domains") or []:
        if not dom.startswith("www."):
            live = f"https://{dom}/"
            break
    # is it serving? (direct uploads are live in seconds)
    up = wait_live(prod, "", seconds=90)
    cc = curl_header(prod, "Cache-Control") if up else None
    say(f"  deployment: {preview or '?'}")
    say(f"  production: {prod} {'— serving' if up else '— not serving yet (check in a minute)'}"
        + (f"  Cache-Control: {cc}" if cc else ""))
    if cc and "no-cache" not in cc and "max-age=0" not in cc:
        say("  WARN HTML is cacheable: copy templates/sites/business/_headers into the repo root")
    if live:
        say(f"  live:       {live}  (custom domain; the same deployment)")
    if key:
        indexnow_submit(meta, name, d, entry, project, key)
    say(f"published {name} @ {sha}: {subject}")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the data layer (B29)

def d1_check():
    """Die with the TODO pointer unless the token can manage D1."""
    try:
        cf_api("GET", "/d1/database?per_page=1")
    except SystemExit:
        die("the toolbelt's Cloudflare token can't manage D1 databases yet (it needs Account · D1 · Edit "
            "beside Pages Edit): TAYLOR-TODO §1 \"Give the Cloudflare token D1\". Nothing was created.")


def data_owner(ws, meta, owner):
    """The one address that signs in to /admin: --owner, else the workspace's contact."""
    owner = (owner or meta.get("contact_email") or "").strip().lower()
    if not re.match(r"^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[a-z]{2,}$", owner):
        die("who signs in to /admin? --owner EMAIL (the owner's address; the sign-in link is emailed there "
            "and it becomes the site's contact address on patchlamp.com)")
    return owner


def wrangler_toml(project, meta, db_name, db_id):
    return f"""# Written by `site data` (claude-tools). The database binding must match the
# site registry (`client doctor` and `db doctor` check it): change it only
# through `site`. `site publish` deploys this file with functions/, so what is
# bound is what's in git. Local preview with a local database:
# `wrangler pages dev` in this folder (secrets for it go in .dev.vars, which is
# never committed); `db --local …` works on the same copy.
name = {json.dumps(project)}
pages_build_output_dir = "."
compatibility_date = "{COMPAT_DATE}"

[vars]
PATCHLAMP_SLUG = {json.dumps(meta["slug"])}
PATCHLAMP_URL = "https://patchlamp.com"
SITE_NAME = {json.dumps(meta["name"])}
TIMEZONE = "America/Denver"

[[d1_databases]]
binding = "DB"
database_name = {json.dumps(db_name)}
database_id = {json.dumps(db_id)}
"""


def binding_problem(repo, entry):
    """None when repo/wrangler.toml binds DB to the registry's database; else what's wrong."""
    d1 = (entry or {}).get("d1") or {}
    if not d1.get("id"):
        return "the registry has no database for it"
    p = repo / "wrangler.toml"
    if not p.exists():
        return "there is no wrangler.toml"
    import tomllib
    try:
        conf = tomllib.loads(p.read_text())
    except tomllib.TOMLDecodeError as exc:
        return f"wrangler.toml doesn't parse ({exc})"
    for b in conf.get("d1_databases") or []:
        if b.get("binding") == "DB":
            if b.get("database_id") != d1["id"] or b.get("database_name") != d1.get("name"):
                return (f"wrangler.toml binds {b.get('database_name')} ({b.get('database_id')}) and the registry "
                        f"says {d1.get('name')} ({d1['id']})")
            return None
    return "wrangler.toml has no DB binding"


def ensure_d1(db_name):
    """(id, created?) for the D1 database with this name, made on first use."""
    found = [x for x in (cf_api("GET", f"/d1/database?name={db_name}") or []) if x.get("name") == db_name]
    if found:
        return found[0]["uuid"], False
    res = cf_api("POST", "/d1/database", {"name": db_name, "primary_location_hint": "wnam"})
    return (res or {}).get("uuid") or "(dry-run)", True


def set_secrets(project, owner):
    """SESSION_SECRET (made here, once, never printed) and ADMIN_EMAIL on the Pages project."""
    p = cf_project(project) or {}
    have = ((p.get("deployment_configs") or {}).get("production") or {}).get("env_vars") or {}
    env = {"ADMIN_EMAIL": {"type": "secret_text", "value": owner}}
    if "SESSION_SECRET" not in have:
        import secrets
        env["SESSION_SECRET"] = {"type": "secret_text", "value": secrets.token_hex(32)}
    cf_api("PATCH", f"/pages/projects/{project}",
           {"deployment_configs": {"production": {"env_vars": env}, "preview": {"env_vars": env}}})
    return sorted(env)


def enable_data(ws, name, owner=None, dry=False):
    """Give ./repos/<name> its own D1 database and the /admin shell. Safe to re-run:
    an existing database, files and session secret are kept."""
    _, meta = workspace()                          # fresh: `newsletter setup` may have written contact_email
    d = repo_dir(ws, name)
    entry = site_entry(meta, name)
    if not entry or entry.get("host") != "cloudflare":
        die(f"repos/{name} isn't a Cloudflare site in the registry; a database needs one (SITE_ADMIN=1 site adopt {name})")
    project = entry["project"]
    owner = data_owner(ws, meta, owner)
    if not dry:
        d1_check()
    say(f"site data {name}: a database for {meta['name']} on Pages project {project}, /admin for {owner}")

    # 1. the database
    db_name = (entry.get("d1") or {}).get("name") or project
    if dry:
        say(f"  would find or create D1 database {db_name} and record its id in {REGISTRY}")
        db_id = (entry.get("d1") or {}).get("id") or "<new id>"
    else:
        db_id, made = ensure_d1(db_name)
        say(f"  {'created' if made else 'found'} D1 database {db_name} ({db_id})")
        reg = registry_load()
        reg.setdefault(meta["slug"], {}).setdefault(name, {})["d1"] = {"name": db_name, "id": db_id, "owner": owner}
        registry_save(reg)

    # 2. the files: the Functions shell and the first migration (never overwriting), the binding
    written = []
    for part in DATA_PARTS:
        for f in sorted((SHELL_DIR / part).rglob("*")):
            if not f.is_file():
                continue
            dest = d / f.relative_to(SHELL_DIR)
            if dest.exists():
                continue
            if not dry:
                dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                shutil.copy(f, dest)
            written.append(str(dest.relative_to(d)))
    toml = wrangler_toml(project, meta, db_name, db_id)
    if not (d / "wrangler.toml").exists() or binding_problem(d, {"d1": {"name": db_name, "id": db_id}}):
        if not dry:
            (d / "wrangler.toml").write_text(toml)
        written.append("wrangler.toml")
    gi = d / ".gitignore"
    lines = gi.read_text().splitlines() if gi.exists() else []
    extra = [x for x in (".wrangler/", ".dev.vars") if x not in lines]
    if extra:
        if not dry:
            gi.write_text("\n".join(lines + extra) + "\n")
        written.append(".gitignore")
    say(f"  {'would write' if dry else 'wrote'} in repos/{name}: {', '.join(written) or 'nothing (all there)'}")

    # 3. the owner: patchlamp.com's contact for this project is where the sign-in link goes
    cmd = [str(NEWSLETTER_BIN), "setup", "--contact", owner]
    if dry:
        say(f"  would run: newsletter setup --contact {owner}   (the sign-in email's address)")
        say(f"  would set Pages secrets SESSION_SECRET (random, never shown) and ADMIN_EMAIL on {project}")
        say(f"  would run: db migrate, then commit, push and publish")
        return
    r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=str(ws))
    if r.returncode != 0:
        say(f"  WARN newsletter setup failed ({(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[:200]}): the sign-in email has "
            f"nowhere to go until `newsletter setup --contact {owner}` works")
    else:
        say(f"  patchlamp.com: {meta['slug']} registered, contact {owner} (the sign-in link is emailed there)")

    # 4. secrets
    names = set_secrets(project, owner)
    say(f"  Pages secrets set on {project}: {', '.join(names)} (values never shown)")

    # 5. tables
    r = subprocess.run([str(DB_BIN), "migrate", "--site", name], capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=str(ws))
    say("  " + (r.stdout.strip() or r.stderr.strip()).replace("\n", "\n  "))
    if r.returncode != 0:
        die("db migrate failed; fix that, then run `site data` again (it keeps what's done)")

    # 6. commit + push (publish is the caller's next step)
    git(d, "add", "-A", "functions", "migrations", "wrangler.toml", ".gitignore")
    _, staged = git(d, "diff", "--cached", "--name-only", check=False)
    if staged.strip():
        git(d, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
            "commit", "-q", "-m", "A database for the site: /admin with an emailed sign-in link, migrations, the D1 binding")
        git(d, "push", "-q")
        say(f"  committed and pushed repos/{name}")


def stripe_post(key, path, fields):
    """POST to Stripe's API with the owner's key (never printed); the JSON answer."""
    import urllib.parse
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{STRIPE_API}/v1{path}", method="POST",
                                 data=urllib.parse.urlencode(fields).encode(),
                                 headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {key}", "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            return json.loads(r.read().decode())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        try:
            msg = json.loads(exc.read().decode()).get("error", {}).get("message")
        except ValueError:
            msg = None
        die(f"Stripe refused it ({exc.code}): {msg or 'no message'}")


STRIPE_VARS = ("STRIPE_SECRET_KEY", "STRIPE_ACCOUNT", "STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET")


def patchlamp_stripe_row(slug):
    """The project's stripe connection row from patchlamp.com (plan 16 § Contract A),
    read the way `connections` reads it, with the relay's shared secret. None if absent."""
    env = read_env()
    secret = os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET") or env.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET")
    if not secret:
        die("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET is not in the toolbelt, so the Stripe connection can't be read")
    base = (os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_URL") or env.get("PATCHLAMP_URL") or "https://patchlamp.com").rstrip("/")
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{base}/internal/relay/projects/{slug}/connections",
                                 headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {secret}", "Accept": "application/json",
                                          "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=25) as r:
            data = json.loads(r.read().decode() or "{}")
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        die(f"patchlamp.com: HTTP {exc.code} reading {slug}'s connections")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
        die(f"patchlamp.com unreachable: {exc}")
    rows = [c for c in data.get("connections") or [] if c.get("kind") == "stripe" and c.get("status") != "revoked"]
    return rows[0] if rows else None


def stripe_account_check(key, acct):
    """GET /v1/account on the connected account with the platform key: reachable, charges on?"""
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{STRIPE_API}/v1/account", headers={
        "Authorization": f"Bearer {key}", "Stripe-Account": acct, "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            return json.loads(r.read().decode())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        try:
            msg = json.loads(exc.read().decode()).get("error", {}).get("message")
        except ValueError:
            msg = None
        die(f"Stripe refused the platform key on {acct} ({exc.code}): {msg or 'no message'}")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
        die(f"Stripe unreachable: {exc}")


def pages_env(project, env):
    cf_api("PATCH", f"/pages/projects/{project}",
           {"deployment_configs": {"production": {"env_vars": env}, "preview": {"env_vars": env}}})


def checkout_connected(a, meta, project):
    """--connected (plan 16 § Contract D): the platform key by NAME, the owner's acct_…,
    and the forward secret patchlamp.com signs the paid event with. No Stripe webhook:
    patchlamp.com's one Connect endpoint is the webhook."""
    key_name = "STRIPE_TEST_KEY" if a.test else "STRIPE_KEY_PATCHLAMP"
    row = patchlamp_stripe_row(meta["slug"])
    if not row:
        die(f"{meta['slug']} has no Stripe connection on patchlamp.com. The owner connects first: the Connect "
            f"Stripe button on patchlamp.com/account, or `CONNECT: stripe | <name>` by text. "
            f"(An owner who won't connect: --key-from, the fallback.)")
    if row.get("status") != "connected":
        need = ", ".join(row.get("requirements") or []) or "the rest of Stripe's onboarding"
        die(f"{meta['slug']}'s Stripe is {row.get('status')}, not connected: Stripe still needs {need}. "
            f"Nothing changed; run this again once `connections` says connected.")
    acct = (row.get("env") or {}).get("STRIPE_CONNECTED_ACCOUNT") or row.get("stripe_account") or row.get("external_id")
    if not acct or not re.match(r"^acct_[A-Za-z0-9]+$", acct):
        die(f"patchlamp.com's stripe row for {meta['slug']} carries no acct_… id")
    fwd = row.get("webhook_secret")
    if not fwd:
        die(f"patchlamp.com's stripe row for {meta['slug']} carries no webhook_secret, so a paid order could never "
            f"be marked paid; nothing changed")
    if row.get("livemode") is True and a.test:
        die(f"{acct} is a live account; drop --test")
    if row.get("livemode") is False and not a.test:
        die(f"{acct} is a test-mode account (a demo?); say --test to use STRIPE_TEST_KEY")
    key = os.environ.get(key_name) or read_env().get(key_name)
    if not key:
        die(f"{key_name} is not in the toolbelt: ~/.config/claude-tools/setenv.sh {key_name} (TAYLOR-TODO §1)")
    want = "_test_" if a.test else "_live_"
    if not key.startswith(("sk", "rk")) or want not in key[:8]:
        die(f"{key_name} doesn't look like a {'test' if a.test else 'live'} Stripe secret key")
    if DRY:
        say(f"  would check {acct} is reachable on {key_name}")
    else:
        info = stripe_account_check(key, acct)
        if not info.get("charges_enabled"):
            die(f"Stripe says {acct} can't take payments yet (charges_enabled false); nothing changed")
        say(f"  {acct} reachable on {key_name}: taking payments")
    env = {"STRIPE_SECRET_KEY": {"type": "secret_text", "value": key},
           "STRIPE_ACCOUNT": {"type": "secret_text", "value": acct},
           "STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET": {"type": "secret_text", "value": fwd}}
    say(f"  {'would set' if DRY else 'setting'} {', '.join(env)} on {project} "
        f"(connected, {'test' if a.test else 'live'} mode, the platform key {key_name}; values never shown; "
        f"no Stripe webhook — patchlamp.com forwards the paid event)")
    if not DRY:
        pages_env(project, env)


def cmd_checkout(a):
    """Switch a site's Checkout on (or off). --connected: the owner's connected
    account on our platform key (the path). --key-from: the owner's own Stripe
    key as a Pages secret, and with --webhook the endpoint Stripe calls when an
    order is paid (the fallback)."""
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    require_admin("checkout")
    ws, meta = workspace()
    entry = site_entry(meta, a.name)
    if not entry or entry.get("host") != "cloudflare" or not (entry.get("d1") or {}).get("id"):
        die(f"repos/{a.name} needs a database and the catalog first: site data {a.name} && db add catalog")
    project = entry["project"]
    if sum(bool(x) for x in (a.off, a.connected, a.key_from)) > 1:
        die("one of --connected, --key-from NAME or --off")
    if a.test and not a.connected:
        die("--test goes with --connected (with --key-from the key itself says test or live)")
    if a.off:
        say(f"  {'would remove' if DRY else 'removing'} {', '.join(STRIPE_VARS)} from {project}")
        if not DRY:
            pages_env(project, {k: None for k in STRIPE_VARS})
    elif a.connected:
        checkout_connected(a, meta, project)
    else:
        if not a.key_from:
            die("--connected (the owner's connected Stripe, the path) or --key-from NAME (the toolbelt key "
                "holding the owner's Stripe secret key, the fallback; setenv.sh NAME first)")
        key = os.environ.get(a.key_from) or read_env().get(a.key_from)
        if not key:
            die(f"{a.key_from} is not in the toolbelt: ~/.config/claude-tools/setenv.sh {a.key_from}")
        mode = "live" if key.startswith(("sk_live_", "rk_live_")) else "test" if key.startswith(("sk_test_", "rk_test_")) else None
        if not mode:
            die(f"{a.key_from} doesn't look like a Stripe secret key (sk_test_… or sk_live_…)")
        if mode == "live" and not a.live:
            die("that's a live key: real cards, real money. Say --live if that's what the owner wants.")
        # STRIPE_ACCOUNT cleared: a site moving off a connection must not send the owner's key to that account
        env = {"STRIPE_SECRET_KEY": {"type": "secret_text", "value": key}, "STRIPE_ACCOUNT": None}
        url = (meta.get("live_url") if meta.get("live_url") and entry.get("domains") else None) or f"https://{pages_host(project)}/"
        if a.webhook:
            hook = f"{url.rstrip('/')}/api/stripe-webhook"
            if DRY:
                say(f"  would create the Stripe webhook {hook} (checkout.session.completed)")
            else:
                res = stripe_post(key, "/webhook_endpoints", {"url": hook, "enabled_events[]": "checkout.session.completed",
                                                              "description": f"{meta['name']} — orders (Patchlamp site)"})
                env["STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET"] = {"type": "secret_text", "value": res["secret"]}
                say(f"  Stripe webhook {res.get('id')} → {hook}")
        say(f"  {'would set' if DRY else 'setting'} {', '.join(k for k, v in env.items() if v)} on {project} "
            f"({mode} mode, the owner's key; values never shown)")
        if not DRY:
            pages_env(project, env)
    # secrets reach a Function only from the next deployment on
    cmd_publish(argparse.Namespace(name=a.name, dry_run=DRY))
    say(f"checkout for {a.name}: {'off' if a.off else 'connected' if a.connected else 'on (owner key)'} — "
        f"`curl -s <url>api/catalog` says checkout (test/live/off) and via (connected/key/off)")


def cmd_data(a):
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    ws, meta = workspace()
    enable_data(ws, a.name, a.owner, dry=a.dry_run)
    if a.dry_run:
        say("dry run: nothing created")
        return
    cmd_publish(argparse.Namespace(name=a.name, dry_run=False))
    entry = site_entry(workspace()[1], a.name) or {}
    url = f"https://{pages_host(entry.get('project', a.name))}/"
    say()
    say(f"database: D1 {(entry.get('d1') or {}).get('name')} bound as DB; `db doctor` checks it")
    say(f"admin:    {url}admin (the owner types their email and gets a one-time link)")
    say(f"next:     db add submissions (a form's posts in a list) or db add records (a list the owner keeps); "
        f"db collections shows them all")


SHELL_OWN = {"functions/_admin/collections.js"}   # the site's own: which lists its /admin shows (db add writes it)


def shell_drift(repo):
    """The /admin shell files in repo that differ from (or are missing against)
    templates/sites/_shell/functions — the generic part: the sign-in, the list
    and entry pages, core.js. Never the site's own views or its migrations."""
    out = []
    for f in sorted((SHELL_DIR / "functions").rglob("*")):
        rel = str(f.relative_to(SHELL_DIR))
        if not f.is_file() or rel in SHELL_OWN:
            continue
        dest = repo / rel
        if not dest.exists() or dest.read_bytes() != f.read_bytes():
            out.append(rel)
    return out


def cmd_shell(a):
    """Bring a site's /admin shell up to the toolbelt's (ROADMAP B41: search,
    filters, totals, CSV, sort, the phone layout arrive on every site this
    way): copy the generic shell files over, commit, push, publish. The
    site's views (functions/_admin/*), its public Functions and its
    migrations are its own and never touched. `--check` only says what's
    behind. Safe to re-run: nothing to copy is nothing done."""
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    ws, meta = workspace()
    reg = registry_load().get(meta["slug"], {})
    names = [a.name] if a.name else [n for n in repos_of(ws) if ((reg.get(n) or {}).get("d1") or {}).get("id")]
    if not names:
        die("no site here has a database, so none has the /admin shell (site data <name> adds both)")
    for name in names:
        d = repo_dir(ws, name)
        if not (d / "functions" / "_lib" / "core.js").exists():
            die(f"repos/{name} has no /admin shell yet: site data {name}")
        drift = shell_drift(d)
        if not drift:
            say(f"repos/{name}: the /admin shell is current")
            continue
        say(f"repos/{name}: {len(drift)} shell file(s) behind the toolbelt: {', '.join(drift)}")
        if a.check:
            continue
        _, dirty = git(d, "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=no", check=False)
        if dirty.strip() and not DRY:
            die(f"repos/{name} has uncommitted changes; commit them first, then site shell {name}")
        for rel in drift:
            if not DRY:
                (d / rel).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                shutil.copy(SHELL_DIR / rel, d / rel)
        git(d, "add", "--", *drift)
        git(d, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
            "commit", "-q", "-m", a.message or "The /admin shell from the toolbelt: search, filters, totals, CSV, sort, the phone layout")
        git(d, "push", "-q")
        cmd_publish(argparse.Namespace(name=name, dry_run=DRY))
    if a.check and any(shell_drift(repo_dir(ws, n)) for n in names):
        sys.exit(1)


def cmd_previews(a):
    """A whole directory tree -> the one previews Pages project, by direct upload (ROADMAP/GROWTH
    B45, plan ~/projects/plans/19-preview-sites.md). Not a client site: there is no workspace, no
    repo and no registry row — `leads preview` owns the tree under
    ~/.local/state/claude-tools/previews and this only puts it on the host. One project holds every
    preview at /<slug>/, so a publish is the whole set and a takedown is a folder deleted and this
    run again. The project's own `_headers` (X-Robots-Tag) and robots.txt come up with the tree."""
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    require_admin("previews")
    src = Path(a.dir).expanduser().resolve()
    project = a.project or PREVIEWS_PROJECT
    if not NAME_RE.match(project):
        die(f"{project!r} is not a valid Pages project name")
    if a.ls:
        p = cf_project(project)
        if not p:
            die(f"no Pages project {project} yet (publish once to make it)")
        say(f"project: {project}")
        say(f"pages host: {pages_host(project)}")
        for dm in cf_domains(project):
            say(f"domain: {dm['name']} {dm.get('status')}")
        dep = p.get("latest_deployment") or {}
        say(f"last publish: {(dep.get('created_on') or '-')[:19]}")
        return
    if not (src / "index.html").exists():
        die(f"{src} has no index.html at its root; `leads preview` writes the tree")
    for want in ("_headers", "robots.txt"):
        if not (src / want).exists():
            die(f"{src} has no {want} — a preview project without it could be indexed; "
                f"`leads preview` writes both (templates/sites/_preview/)")
    if "noindex" not in (src / "_headers").read_text():
        die(f"{src}/_headers does not say noindex; refusing to publish previews that can be indexed")
    if not DRY and not cf_project(project) and not a.yes:
        die(f"there is no Pages project {project} yet, so this is the first time a preview naming a real "
            f"business would be on the internet. That is Taylor's word to give (GROWTH § 10, TAYLOR-TODO §1 "
            f"\"Preview sites\"). With it: the same command plus --yes.")
    cf_ensure_project(project)
    n = sum(1 for p in src.rglob("*") if p.is_file())
    slugs = sorted(d.name for d in src.iterdir() if d.is_dir() and (d / "index.html").exists())
    say(f"publishing {src} ({n} files, {len(slugs)} preview(s)) -> {project}")
    code, log = wrangler("pages", "deploy", str(src), "--project-name", project, "--branch", "main",
                         "--commit-dirty=true", "--commit-message", f"{len(slugs)} previews", cwd=src.parent)
    if DRY:
        say("dry run: nothing published")
        say(f"pages host: {pages_host(project)}")
        return
    if code != 0:
        die("wrangler pages deploy failed:\n" + "\n".join(log.splitlines()[-8:]))
    host = pages_host(project)
    say(f"pages host: {host}")
    for dm in cf_domains(project):
        say(f"domain: {dm['name']} {dm.get('status')}")
    prod = f"https://{host}/"
    up = wait_live(prod, "", seconds=90)
    xr = curl_header(prod, "X-Robots-Tag") if up else None
    say(f"  {prod} {'— serving' if up else '— not serving yet (check in a minute)'}"
        + (f"  X-Robots-Tag: {xr}" if xr else ""))
    if up and not (xr and "noindex" in xr):
        say("  WARN the host is not sending X-Robots-Tag: noindex — check _headers reached the root")
    for s in slugs:
        say(f"  {prod}{s}/")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the watch (B72)
#
# `site watch` fetches every live client site in the registry and every live preview, every 15 minutes
# (site-watch.timer), and keeps the record in the relay's state/uptime.json — the relay reads it, this
# writes it (plan ~/projects/plans/30-site-watch.md § Contracts). A check is: DNS (IPv4) resolving into
# Cloudflare's ranges, a TLS handshake the system trusts (and the days left on the certificate), then
# the home page answering 200 with one of the template's markers in it. Two failed checks in a row are
# an outage: `outage` is set, Taylor gets one `notify` with the evidence and one TAYLOR-TODO § 7 entry,
# and the relay's schedule tick texts the owner once (relay/nudges.py `site_down`). One failed check is
# a blip: `fails` goes to 1 and nothing is said. The first good check after an outage closes it into
# `outages` (the weekly report's line) and Taylor hears it once more; the owner's "it's back" is the
# relay's `site_back`. Once a week a custom domain's expiry is read by RDAP; inside 30 days it is a § 7
# entry (the relay texts the owner, `domain_expiry`, with the registrar named). A preview has no owner:
# it is reported to Taylor and never texted, and one past its 30 days that is still up is reported too.

WATCH_FILE = Path(os.environ.get("SITE_WATCH_FILE") or Path.home() / "projects/sms-relay/state/uptime.json")
WATCH_RELAY_DIR = Path(os.environ.get("RELAY_DIR") or Path.home() / "projects/sms-relay")
WATCH_TODO = Path(os.environ.get("TAYLOR_TODO") or Path.home() / "projects/TAYLOR-TODO.md")
WATCH_PREVIEWS = Path(os.environ.get("LEADS_PREVIEWS") or Path.home() / ".local/state/claude-tools/previews")
WATCH_INTERVAL = 15                         # minutes; site-watch.timer
WATCH_CONFIRM = 2                           # failed checks in a row before anyone hears of it
WATCH_KEEP_DAYS = 60                        # outages and gaps kept this long
WATCH_GAP_MINUTES = 45                      # two checks further apart than this = the watch was off
WATCH_RDAP_DAYS = 7                         # a domain's expiry is read once a week
WATCH_DOMAIN_WARN = 30                      # days before expiry that it becomes a § 7 entry and a text
WATCH_CERT_WARN = 7                         # days left on a certificate that doctor calls out
WATCH_TIMEOUT = 20
WATCH_RDAP = (os.environ.get("SITE_WATCH_RDAP") or "https://rdap.org/domain/").rstrip("/") + "/"
WATCH_MARKERS = ("patchlamp-badge", 'class="site-header"', 'class="wordmark')   # any one: a page of ours
PREVIEW_MARKERS = ("preview-note", "A preview Patchlamp made for")
CLOUDFLARE_V4 = ("173.245.48.0/20", "103.21.244.0/22", "103.22.200.0/22", "103.31.4.0/22", "141.101.64.0/18",
                 "108.162.192.0/18", "190.93.240.0/20", "188.114.96.0/20", "197.234.240.0/22", "198.41.128.0/17",
                 "162.158.0.0/15", "104.16.0.0/13", "104.24.0.0/14", "172.64.0.0/13", "131.0.72.0/22")
WATCH_PRETEND = set()                       # --pretend-down: a rehearsal, never set by the timer


def watch_now():
    return datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().replace(microsecond=0)


def watch_iso(t):
    return t.isoformat() if t else None


def watch_parse(s):
    try:
        return datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(s) if s else None
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None


def watch_targets():
    """Every site to check: [{key, kind, slug, repo, project, url, host, markers, domain}]. Clients from the
    registry (Cloudflare rows); previews from leads' manifests, once the previews project has been published."""
    out = []
    for slug, rows in sorted(registry_load().items()):
        for repo, e in sorted(rows.items()):
            if e.get("host") != "cloudflare" or e.get("watch") is False:
                continue
            host = site_host(e, e["project"]) if e.get("domains") else (e.get("pages_host") or f"{e['project']}.pages.dev")
            custom = host if e.get("domains") else None
            out.append({"key": f"{slug}/{repo}", "kind": "client", "slug": slug, "repo": repo, "project": e["project"],
                        "url": f"https://{host}/", "host": host, "domain": custom,
                        "markers": [e["watch_marker"]] if e.get("watch_marker") else list(WATCH_MARKERS)})
    try:
        proj = json.loads((WATCH_PREVIEWS / "project.json").read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        proj = None
    if proj:                                # no project.json = previews never published: nothing live to watch
        phost = proj.get("domain") or proj.get("pages_host")
        for p in sorted((WATCH_PREVIEWS / "meta").glob("*.json")) if (WATCH_PREVIEWS / "meta").is_dir() else []:
            try:
                m = json.loads(p.read_text())
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if not m.get("slug") or not phost:
                continue
            out.append({"key": f"preview/{m['slug']}", "kind": "preview", "slug": m["slug"], "repo": None,
                        "project": proj.get("project") or PREVIEWS_PROJECT, "url": f"https://{phost}/{m['slug']}/",
                        "host": phost, "domain": None, "markers": list(PREVIEW_MARKERS),
                        "expires": m.get("expires"), "claimed": m.get("claimed"), "name": m.get("name")})
    return out


def watch_resolve(host):
    """IPv4 addresses for host (the machine's resolver is slow on AAAA; memory: headless-browser-shot)."""
    import socket
    try:
        return sorted({ai[4][0] for ai in socket.getaddrinfo(host, 443, socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)})
    except OSError:
        return []


def watch_on_cloudflare(ip):
    import ipaddress
    try:
        a = ipaddress.ip_address(ip)
    except ValueError:
        return False
    return any(a in ipaddress.ip_network(n) for n in CLOUDFLARE_V4)


def watch_fetch(host, ip, path="/", hops=3):
    """GET https://host/path over ip, verifying the certificate for host. -> (status, body, cert_days, error).
    Follows up to `hops` redirects on the same host."""
    import http.client
    import socket
    import ssl
    ctx = ssl.create_default_context()

    class Conn(http.client.HTTPSConnection):
        def connect(self):
            self.sock = ctx.wrap_socket(socket.create_connection((ip, 443), WATCH_TIMEOUT), server_hostname=host)

    cert_days = None
    for _ in range(hops + 1):
        c = Conn(host, 443, timeout=WATCH_TIMEOUT)
        try:
            c.request("GET", path, headers={"User-Agent": "claude-tools site watch", "Cache-Control": "no-cache"})
            if cert_days is None and c.sock:
                na = (c.sock.getpeercert() or {}).get("notAfter")
                if na:
                    cert_days = int((ssl.cert_time_to_seconds(na) - time.time()) // 86400)
            r = c.getresponse()
            body = r.read(1_000_000).decode("utf-8", "replace")
            loc = r.getheader("Location") or ""
        except ssl.SSLError as exc:
            return 0, "", cert_days, f"certificate: {getattr(exc, 'verify_message', None) or exc.reason or exc}"
        except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as exc:
            return 0, "", cert_days, f"no answer: {exc}"
        finally:
            c.close()
        if r.status in (301, 302, 303, 307, 308) and loc:
            import urllib.parse
            u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(urllib.parse.urljoin(f"https://{host}{path}", loc))
            if u.hostname and u.hostname != host:
                return r.status, "", cert_days, f"redirects away to {u.hostname}"
            path = (u.path or "/") + (f"?{u.query}" if u.query else "")
            continue
        return r.status, body, cert_days, ""
    return 0, "", cert_days, "too many redirects"


def watch_probe(t):
    """One check of one target -> the last_check dict."""
    started = time.time()
    out = {"at": watch_iso(watch_now()), "ok": False, "status": 0, "marker": False, "dns": "", "cert_days": None,
           "ms": 0, "problem": ""}
    if t["key"] in WATCH_PRETEND or t["slug"] in WATCH_PRETEND:
        out.update(dns="skipped", problem="pretend-down: a rehearsal (site watch --pretend-down), not a real fault")
        return out
    ips = watch_resolve(t["host"])
    if not ips:
        out.update(dns="none", problem=f"{t['host']} does not resolve (no DNS answer)")
        return out
    cf = [ip for ip in ips if watch_on_cloudflare(ip)]
    out["dns"] = "cloudflare" if cf else "elsewhere:" + ",".join(ips[:3])
    if not cf:
        out["problem"] = f"{t['host']} points away from Cloudflare ({', '.join(ips[:3])})"
        return out
    path = "/" + t["url"].split("/", 3)[3] if t["url"].count("/") > 3 else "/"
    status, body, cert_days, err = watch_fetch(t["host"], cf[0], path)
    out.update(status=status, cert_days=cert_days, ms=int((time.time() - started) * 1000))
    if err:
        out["problem"] = err
        return out
    out["marker"] = any(m in body for m in t["markers"])
    if status != 200:
        out["problem"] = f"HTTP {status}"
    elif not out["marker"]:
        out["problem"] = "HTTP 200 but not our page (no template marker in it)"
    else:
        out["ok"] = True
    return out


def watch_registrable(domain):
    parts = domain.lower().strip(".").split(".")
    two = {"co.uk", "org.uk", "com.au", "net.au", "co.nz", "com.mx", "com.br"}
    n = 3 if len(parts) >= 3 and ".".join(parts[-2:]) in two else 2
    return ".".join(parts[-n:])


def watch_rdap(domain):
    """-> {name, expires, registrar, error} from RDAP (rdap.org redirects to the registry's server)."""
    name = watch_registrable(domain)
    row = {"name": name, "expires": None, "registrar": None, "error": ""}
    req = urllib.request.Request(WATCH_RDAP + name, headers={"Accept": "application/rdap+json",
                                                             "User-Agent": "claude-tools site watch"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=WATCH_TIMEOUT) as r:
            data = json.loads(r.read(2_000_000).decode("utf-8", "replace"))
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        row["error"] = f"RDAP: {exc}"
        return row
    for ev in data.get("events") or []:
        if ev.get("eventAction") == "expiration":
            row["expires"] = (ev.get("eventDate") or "")[:10] or None
    for ent in data.get("entities") or []:
        if "registrar" in (ent.get("roles") or []):
            for item in ((ent.get("vcardArray") or [None, []])[1] or []):
                if item and item[0] == "fn":
                    row["registrar"] = item[3]
    if not row["expires"]:
        row["error"] = "RDAP gave no expiration date"
    return row


def watch_notify(text):
    """One message to Taylor (the relay's `notify`). Never fails the watch."""
    exe = shutil.which("notify") or str(HERE / "bin" / "notify")
    try:
        subprocess.run([exe, text], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60, check=False)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:
        say(f"  notify failed: {exc}")


def watch_file_todo(entry):
    """One entry under TAYLOR-TODO § 7, through the escalation triage's own helper
    (relay/escalate.py append_todo) so both file the same way. False when it couldn't."""
    py = WATCH_RELAY_DIR / ".venv" / "bin" / "python"
    code = ("import sys; from pathlib import Path; from relay.escalate import append_todo; "
            "sys.exit(0 if append_todo(sys.stdin.read(), Path(sys.argv[1])) else 1)")
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([str(py if py.exists() else sys.executable), "-c", code, str(WATCH_TODO)], input=entry,
                           cwd=str(WATCH_RELAY_DIR), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60, check=False)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:
        say(f"  TODO § 7 not filed: {exc}")
        return False
    if r.returncode != 0:
        say(f"  TODO § 7 not filed: {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-200:] or 'no TAYLOR-TODO.md'}")
    return r.returncode == 0


def watch_load():
    try:
        data = json.loads(WATCH_FILE.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        data = {}
    data.setdefault("version", 1)
    data.setdefault("sites", {})
    return data


def watch_save(data):
    WATCH_FILE.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = WATCH_FILE.with_suffix(".json.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=1, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
    tmp.replace(WATCH_FILE)


def watch_minutes(a, b):
    return max(0, int(round((b - a).total_seconds() / 60)))


def watch_clock(t):
    return t.strftime("%a %-d %b %-H:%M")


def watch_outage_todo(t, row, now):
    o = row["outage"]
    since = watch_parse(o["since"])
    who = ("Patch texts the owner once on the relay's next schedule tick (or you, where the project has no "
           "client number)")
    ws = f"~/projects/clients/{t['slug']}"
    return (f"- [ ] **{t['slug']}'s site is down: {t['url']} (since {watch_clock(since)}).** Two checks in a row "
            f"failed: {o['problem']}. {who}; nothing has been changed.\n"
            f"  - **1.** Look at it: `shot {t['url']}` and `cd {ws} && site doctor`.\n"
            f"  - **2.** Serving nothing or a 404: `cd {ws} && site publish {t['repo']}` puts HEAD back up. "
            f"Pointing away from Cloudflare: the domain's DNS records (`SITE_ADMIN=1 site domain {t['repo']}` prints "
            f"the two lines). A certificate fault: the Pages project's custom domains in the Cloudflare dashboard.\n"
            f"  - **Then:** the next check (every {WATCH_INTERVAL} minutes) sees it up, Patch texts the owner it's back, "
            f"and this can be ticked.\n"
            f"  - **Details:** outage {o['id']}; last check {row['last_check']['at']}: status "
            f"{row['last_check']['status']}, DNS {row['last_check']['dns'] or '-'}, certificate "
            f"{row['last_check']['cert_days'] if row['last_check']['cert_days'] is not None else '-'} day(s) left. "
            f"`site watch --once` re-checks now.\n"
            f"  _(site watch, {now.date().isoformat()})_\n")


def watch_domain_todo(t, d, now):
    reg = d.get("registrar") or "the registrar (RDAP didn't name one)"
    return (f"- [ ] **{d['name']} expires {d['expires']} ({d['days_left']} days): {t['slug']}'s site goes dark with "
            f"it.** Registered with {reg}. Patch texts the owner once, naming the registrar.\n"
            f"  - **1.** Ask the owner whether they renew it themselves (it's in their name at {reg}), or whether "
            f"we do.\n"
            f"  - **2.** Once it's renewed, `site watch --once --rdap` reads the new date.\n"
            f"  - **Then:** the entry can be ticked; the weekly RDAP read stops warning.\n"
            f"  - **Details:** read by RDAP {d.get('checked_at')}; site {t['url']}.\n"
            f"  _(site watch, {now.date().isoformat()})_\n")


def watch_run(dry=False, rdap_now=False, only=None):
    """One pass. Returns (data, events) — events are the lines Taylor is told."""
    now = watch_now()
    data = watch_load()
    sites = data["sites"]
    events, todos = [], []
    targets = [t for t in watch_targets() if not only or t["key"] in only or t["slug"] in only]
    started = time.time()
    for t in targets:
        row = sites.setdefault(t["key"], {"watched_since": watch_iso(now), "fails": 0, "outage": None,
                                          "outages": [], "gaps": [], "filed": {}, "state": "pending"})
        row.update(kind=t["kind"], slug=t["slug"], repo=t["repo"], project=t["project"], url=t["url"],
                   host=t["host"], markers=t["markers"])
        for k, v in (("outages", []), ("gaps", []), ("filed", {}), ("fails", 0), ("outage", None)):
            row.setdefault(k, v)
        prev = watch_parse((row.get("last_check") or {}).get("at"))
        if prev and (now - prev).total_seconds() > WATCH_GAP_MINUTES * 60:
            row["gaps"].append({"from": watch_iso(prev), "to": watch_iso(now)})
        chk = watch_probe(t)
        row["last_check"] = chk
        preview_note = t["kind"] == "preview"
        if chk["ok"]:
            row.setdefault("first_up", chk["at"])
            if row.get("outage"):
                o = row["outage"]
                since = watch_parse(o["since"])
                closed = dict(o, until=chk["at"], minutes=watch_minutes(since, now))
                row["outages"].append(closed)
                events.append(f"BACK {t['key']} {t['url']} after {closed['minutes']} min (down since "
                              f"{watch_clock(since)})" + ("" if preview_note else "; Patch texts the owner it's back"))
            row.update(fails=0, fail_since=None, outage=None, state="up")
        else:
            row["fails"] = int(row.get("fails") or 0) + 1
            if row["fails"] == 1:
                row["fail_since"] = chk["at"]
            confirmable = t["kind"] == "client" or row.get("first_up")   # a preview never once up isn't an outage
            if row["fails"] >= WATCH_CONFIRM and not row.get("outage") and confirmable:
                since = row.get("fail_since") or chk["at"]
                row["outage"] = {"id": f"{t['key']}@{since}", "since": since, "confirmed_at": chk["at"],
                                 "problem": chk["problem"]}
                events.append(f"DOWN {t['key']} {t['url']}: {chk['problem']} (failing since "
                              f"{watch_clock(watch_parse(since))})" + (" — a preview: reported, not texted"
                                                                       if preview_note else ""))
                fkey = "outage:" + row["outage"]["id"]
                if t["kind"] == "client" and fkey not in row["filed"]:
                    todos.append((row, fkey, watch_outage_todo(t, row, now)))
            if row.get("outage"):
                row["outage"]["problem"] = chk["problem"]
            row["state"] = "down" if row.get("outage") else ("pending" if not row.get("first_up") else "up")
        if t["kind"] == "preview" and t.get("expires") and not t.get("claimed"):
            try:
                left = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(t["expires"]) - now.date()).days
            except ValueError:
                left = None
            if left is not None and left < 0:
                row["state"] = "expired" if chk["ok"] else row["state"]
                fkey = f"expired:{t['expires']}"
                if chk["ok"] and fkey not in row["filed"]:
                    events.append(f"EXPIRED {t['key']} ({t.get('name') or t['slug']}) passed its 30 days on "
                                  f"{t['expires']} and is still up: `leads preview sweep` takes it down — reported, "
                                  f"not texted (a preview has no owner)")
                    row["filed"][fkey] = watch_iso(now)
        if t.get("domain"):
            d = row.get("domain") or {}
            last = watch_parse(d.get("checked_at"))
            if rdap_now or not last or d.get("host") != t["domain"] or (now - last).days >= WATCH_RDAP_DAYS:
                d = dict(watch_rdap(t["domain"]), host=t["domain"], checked_at=watch_iso(now))
            if d.get("expires"):
                d["days_left"] = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(d["expires"]) - now.date()).days
            row["domain"] = d
            if d.get("expires") and d["days_left"] <= WATCH_DOMAIN_WARN:
                fkey = f"domain:{d['name']}:{d['expires']}"
                if fkey not in row["filed"]:
                    events.append(f"DOMAIN {d['name']} ({t['key']}) expires {d['expires']}, {d['days_left']} days, "
                                  f"registered with {d.get('registrar') or 'unknown'}; Patch texts the owner")
                    todos.append((row, fkey, watch_domain_todo(t, d, now)))
        cut = now - datetime.timedelta(days=WATCH_KEEP_DAYS)
        row["outages"] = [o for o in row["outages"] if (watch_parse(o.get("until")) or now) >= cut]
        row["gaps"] = [g for g in row["gaps"] if (watch_parse(g.get("to")) or now) >= cut]
    if not only:                             # a full pass: a preview swept away is no longer watched
        keys = {t["key"] for t in targets}
        for key in [k for k, r in sites.items() if k not in keys]:
            if sites[key].get("kind") == "preview":
                del sites[key]
            else:
                sites[key].update(state="unwatched", outage=None)   # retired: the history stays, nobody is texted
    data.update(updated=watch_iso(now), interval_minutes=WATCH_INTERVAL,
                last_run={"at": watch_iso(now), "checked": len(targets),
                          "down": sum(1 for t in targets if sites[t["key"]].get("outage")),
                          "took_s": round(time.time() - started, 1), "pretend": sorted(WATCH_PRETEND) or None})
    if dry:
        return data, events
    for row, fkey, entry in todos:
        if watch_file_todo(entry):
            row["filed"][fkey] = watch_iso(now)
    watch_save(data)                         # before the notify: the relay's tick may already be reading it
    if events:
        watch_notify("Site watch:\n" + "\n".join(events)
                     + ("\n(TAYLOR-TODO § 7 has the steps.)" if todos else ""))
    return data, events


def watch_scope():
    """Inside a client workspace, the watch shows that client's own sites and nothing else (VISION rule 4)."""
    p = Path.cwd() / ".client.json"
    if not p.exists():
        return None
    try:
        return json.loads(p.read_text()).get("slug") or "?"
    except ValueError:
        return "?"


def cmd_watch(a):
    """`site watch`: one pass over every live site (the timer's job), or the watch as it stands."""
    import fcntl
    scope = watch_scope()
    if scope:
        a.site = [scope]
    if not a.once and not a.dry_run and not a.pretend_down:
        return watch_show(a)
    if scope and os.environ.get("SITE_ADMIN") != "1":
        die("a pass of the watch runs from the timer or Taylor's session, not a client workspace "
            "(`site watch` alone shows this client's sites)")
    WATCH_PRETEND.update(a.pretend_down or [])
    WATCH_FILE.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(WATCH_FILE.with_suffix(".lock"), "w") as lock:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError:
            die("another site watch is running")
        data, events = watch_run(dry=a.dry_run, rdap_now=a.rdap, only=set(a.site or []))
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(data, indent=1, sort_keys=True))
        return
    watch_print(data, only=set(a.site or []))
    for e in events:
        say(("  would say: " if a.dry_run else "  told Taylor: ") + e)
    if a.dry_run:
        say("dry run: nothing written, nobody told")


def watch_print(data, only=None):
    lr = data.get("last_run") or {}
    say(f"site watch: {lr.get('checked', 0)} site(s) checked at {(lr.get('at') or '-')[:16]}, "
        f"{lr.get('down', 0)} down" + (f"  [PRETEND DOWN: {', '.join(lr['pretend'])}]" if lr.get("pretend") else ""))
    for key, row in sorted((data.get("sites") or {}).items()):
        if only and key not in only and row.get("slug") not in only:
            continue
        c = row.get("last_check") or {}
        dom = row.get("domain") or {}
        say(f"  {key:<44} {row.get('state', '?'):<8} {(c.get('at') or '-')[:16]}  "
            + (f"HTTP {c.get('status')} {c.get('ms')}ms cert {c.get('cert_days')}d" if c.get("ok") else c.get("problem") or "-")
            + (f"  domain {dom['name']} {dom.get('days_left')}d" if dom.get("expires") else "")
            + (f"  ({len(row.get('outages') or [])} outage(s) in {WATCH_KEEP_DAYS}d)" if row.get("outages") else ""))


def watch_show(a):
    if not WATCH_FILE.exists():
        say(f"no watch yet ({WATCH_FILE}); `site watch --once` runs one pass, site-watch.timer every {WATCH_INTERVAL} min")
        return
    data = watch_load()
    if a.json:
        only = set(a.site or [])
        if only:
            data = dict(data, sites={k: r for k, r in data["sites"].items() if k in only or r.get("slug") in only})
        print(json.dumps(data, indent=1, sort_keys=True))
        return
    watch_print(data, only=set(a.site or []))


def watch_doctor(fail):
    """`site doctor`'s lines for the watch: the timer, the last pass, every site's last check."""
    say("== watch (B72)")
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "is-active", "site-watch.timer"], capture_output=True,
                           text=True, timeout=10, check=False)
        state = r.stdout.strip() or "unknown"
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        state = "unknown (no systemctl)"
    say(f"  site-watch.timer: {state}" + ("" if state == "active" else
        " (ln -s ~/projects/claude-tools/systemd/site-watch.{service,timer} ~/.config/systemd/user/ && "
        "systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user enable --now site-watch.timer)"))
    if not WATCH_FILE.exists():
        say(f"  no checks yet ({WATCH_FILE})")
        return
    data = watch_load()
    scope = watch_scope()
    lr = watch_parse((data.get("last_run") or {}).get("at"))
    age = int((watch_now() - lr).total_seconds() // 60) if lr else None
    fresh = age is not None and age <= 3 * WATCH_INTERVAL
    text = (f"last pass: {(lr.isoformat()[:16] if lr else 'never')}" + (f" ({age} min ago)" if age is not None else "")
            + ("" if fresh else " — the watch has stopped"))
    fail(text) if not fresh else say("  " + text)
    seen = set(data.get("sites") or {})
    for t in watch_targets():
        if scope and t["slug"] != scope:
            continue
        if t["key"] not in seen:
            say(f"  {t['key']}: not checked yet (the next pass picks it up)")
    for key, row in sorted((data.get("sites") or {}).items()):
        if scope and (row.get("kind") != "client" or row.get("slug") != scope):
            continue
        c = row.get("last_check") or {}
        text = (f"{key}: {row.get('state')} · last check {(c.get('at') or '-')[:16]} "
                + ("ok" if c.get("ok") else f"FAILED: {c.get('problem')}"))
        if c.get("cert_days") is not None and c["cert_days"] <= WATCH_CERT_WARN:
            text += f" · certificate {c['cert_days']} day(s) left"
        dom = row.get("domain") or {}
        if dom.get("expires"):
            text += f" · {dom['name']} expires {dom['expires']} ({dom.get('registrar') or 'registrar unknown'})"
        fail(text) if row.get("outage") else say("  " + text)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mail (B75)
#
# Plan ~/projects/plans/34-email.md. Every hosted client site has an address Patch
# answers: <slug>@mail.patchlamp.com by default, `hello@<their domain>` for a domain
# on our Cloudflare account whose apex has no mail. The mailbox itself lives on
# patchlamp.com (GET/PUT /internal/relay/projects/{slug}/mailbox, § Contract C3); the
# site shows it in its Contact block as <a data-mail href="mailto:…">…</a>, filled
# by `site new` and rewritten by `site mail`. Mail in and out goes through Resend on
# every domain; the relay polls the app, the app sends. This tool never sends mail.

MAIL_DOMAIN = os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_MAIL_DOMAIN") or "mail.patchlamp.com"
MAIL_ZONE = "patchlamp.com"                         # mail.patchlamp.com's records live at Porkbun, in this zone
RESEND_API = (os.environ.get("RESEND_API_BASE") or "https://api.resend.com").rstrip("/")   # env: tests only
MAIL_LINK = re.compile(r'<a\b(?=[^>]*\bdata-mail\b)[^>]*>.*?</a>', re.S)
MAIL_LINE = re.compile(r'(?m)^[ \t]*(?:<(li|p)\b[^>]*>)?[ \t]*<a\b(?=[^>]*\bdata-mail\b)[^>]*>[^<]*</a>'
                       r'[ \t]*(?:</(?:li|p)>)?[ \t]*\r?\n')
MAIL_NOT_YET = "the app doesn't have mail yet (patchlamp.com has no /internal/relay/…/mail routes; the B75 app half isn't deployed)"


def mail_default(slug):
    return f"{slug}@{MAIL_DOMAIN}"


class AppMissing(Exception):
    """patchlamp.com answered 404 for a route it doesn't have (yet)."""


def app_call(method, path, body=None):
    """(status, json) from patchlamp.com's relay API with the shared secret, never printed.
    Raises AppMissing when the route itself isn't there; dies on anything else unexpected."""
    env = read_env()
    secret = os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET") or env.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET")
    if not secret:
        die("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET is not in the toolbelt, so the mailbox on patchlamp.com can't be read")
    base = (os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_URL") or env.get("PATCHLAMP_URL") or "https://patchlamp.com").rstrip("/")
    data = json.dumps(body).encode() if body is not None else None
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{base}{path}", data=data, method=method,
                                 headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {secret}", "Accept": "application/json",
                                          "Content-Type": "application/json", "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=25) as r:
            return r.status, json.loads(r.read().decode() or "{}")
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        raw = exc.read().decode(errors="replace")
        try:
            payload = json.loads(raw)
        except ValueError:
            payload = None
        msg = (payload or {}).get("error") or (payload or {}).get("message") or raw[:200]
        if exc.code == 404 and (payload is None or "could not be found" in str(msg)):
            raise AppMissing(path)
        return exc.code, {"error": msg, **(payload if isinstance(payload, dict) else {})}
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
        die(f"patchlamp.com unreachable: {exc}")


def mailbox_get(slug):
    """The project's mailbox from patchlamp.com ({} when it has none). Dies plainly when
    the app has no mail routes yet."""
    try:
        code, data = app_call("GET", f"/internal/relay/projects/{slug}/mailbox")
    except AppMissing:
        die(MAIL_NOT_YET)
    if code == 404:
        return {}
    if code != 200:
        die(f"patchlamp.com: HTTP {code} reading {slug}'s mailbox: {data.get('error')}")
    return data.get("mailbox") or {}


def mailbox_put(slug, body):
    """PUT the mailbox (C3). `body` is exactly what goes over the wire."""
    if DRY:
        say(f"  would PUT /internal/relay/projects/{slug}/mailbox {json.dumps(body)}")
        return dict(body)
    try:
        code, data = app_call("PUT", f"/internal/relay/projects/{slug}/mailbox", body)
    except AppMissing:
        die(MAIL_NOT_YET)
    if code not in (200, 201):
        die(f"patchlamp.com refused the mailbox ({code}): {data.get('error')}")
    return data.get("mailbox") or dict(body)


def mail_for_new_site(slug):
    """What {{MAIL}} is filled with by `site new`: the app's mailbox if it has one, else
    the default the app gives every client project on its next sync. '' for a mailbox
    that's off (the Contact line is then left out). Never dies: a site is made either way."""
    try:
        code, data = app_call("GET", f"/internal/relay/projects/{slug}/mailbox")
        box = (data.get("mailbox") or {}) if code == 200 else {}
    except (AppMissing, SystemExit, Exception):             # noqa: BLE001 - a new site never waits on mail
        box = {}
    if box.get("status") == "off":
        return ""
    return box.get("address") or mail_default(slug)


def fill_mail(text, address):
    """{{MAIL}} filled; with no address, the Contact line that holds it is dropped so the
    page still reads cleanly."""
    if not address:
        text = MAIL_LINE.sub("", text)
        text = MAIL_LINK.sub("", text)
    return text.replace("{{MAIL}}", address)


def mail_links(d):
    """{relpath: [the data-mail links]} for every page of a repo."""
    out = {}
    for p in sorted(d.rglob("*.html")):
        rel = p.relative_to(d)
        if rel.parts[0] in (".git", "functions", "node_modules", "shots"):
            continue
        try:
            found = MAIL_LINK.findall(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            continue
        if found:
            out[str(rel)] = found
    return out


def mail_link_address(link):
    m = re.search(r'href="mailto:([^"?]*)', link)
    return m.group(1) if m else ""


def rewrite_mail(d, address):
    """Point every data-mail link in the repo at `address`; the pages changed."""
    changed = []
    for rel in mail_links(d):
        p = d / rel
        text = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")

        def one(m):
            link = m.group(0)
            link = re.sub(r'href="mailto:[^"]*"', f'href="mailto:{address}"', link, count=1)
            return re.sub(r'>[^<]*</a>$', f'>{address}</a>', link)
        out = MAIL_LINK.sub(one, text)
        if out != text:
            if not DRY:
                p.write_text(out, encoding="utf-8")
            changed.append(rel)
    return changed


def resend_key():
    key = os.environ.get("RESEND_API_KEY") or read_env().get("RESEND_API_KEY")
    if not key:
        die("RESEND_API_KEY is not in the toolbelt (~/.config/claude-tools/setenv.sh RESEND_API_KEY)")
    return key


def resend(method, path, body=None, ok=(200, 201)):
    """One Resend API call with the toolbelt key (never printed). (status, json)."""
    data = json.dumps(body).encode() if body is not None else None
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{RESEND_API}{path}", data=data, method=method,
                                 headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {resend_key()}", "Content-Type": "application/json",
                                          "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            return r.status, json.loads(r.read().decode() or "{}")
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        raw = exc.read().decode(errors="replace")
        try:
            payload = json.loads(raw)
        except ValueError:
            payload = {"message": raw[:200]}
        if exc.code in ok:
            return exc.code, payload
        die(f"Resend {method} {path}: HTTP {exc.code}: {payload.get('message') or payload.get('name') or raw[:200]}")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
        die(f"Resend unreachable: {exc}")


def resend_domain(name):
    """The Resend domain object (with its records) for `name`, or None."""
    _, data = resend("GET", "/domains")
    for dom in data.get("data") or []:
        if dom.get("name") == name:
            _, full = resend("GET", f"/domains/{dom['id']}")
            return full
    return None


def resend_ensure_domain(name):
    """The Resend domain for `name` with sending and receiving on: made if absent, receiving
    switched on if it was off. Returns the domain with its records."""
    dom = resend_domain(name)
    if dom is None:
        if DRY:
            say(f"  would create the Resend domain {name} (sending + receiving)")
            return None
        code, dom = resend("POST", "/domains", {"name": name, "capabilities": {"sending": "enabled", "receiving": "enabled"}},
                           ok=(200, 201, 403, 422))
        if code not in (200, 201):
            die(f"Resend won't add {name} ({code}): {dom.get('message') or dom.get('name')}. The free plan holds 3 domains: "
                f"delete the retired plateful.fyi / platefuloffers.fyi in Resend, or move to Pro (TAYLOR-TODO §1 \"Email for Patch\").")
        say(f"  created the Resend domain {name} (sending + receiving)")
        _, dom = resend("GET", f"/domains/{dom['id']}")
    elif (dom.get("capabilities") or {}).get("receiving") != "enabled":
        if DRY:
            say(f"  would switch receiving on for the Resend domain {name}")
        else:
            resend("PATCH", f"/domains/{dom['id']}", {"capabilities": {"receiving": "enabled"}})
            say(f"  switched receiving on for the Resend domain {name}")
            _, dom = resend("GET", f"/domains/{dom['id']}")
    else:
        say(f"  Resend domain {name}: already there ({dom.get('status')}), receiving on")
    return dom


def record_fqdn(name, zone):
    """A Resend record name (relative to the zone, '@' or '' for the apex) as a full name."""
    name = (name or "").strip().rstrip(".").lower()
    if name in ("", "@", zone):
        return zone
    return name if name.endswith("." + zone) else f"{name}.{zone}"


def record_relative(fqdn, zone):
    return "@" if fqdn == zone else fqdn[: -(len(zone) + 1)]


def dig(rtype, name):
    """What public DNS answers (IPv4 transport: DNS is slow over v6 here), as a list."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["dig", "-4", "+short", rtype, name], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=15)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return []
    return [l.strip() for l in r.stdout.splitlines() if l.strip()]


def dns_matches(rec, zone):
    """True when public DNS already answers what the Resend record asks for."""
    got = [g.lower().rstrip(".").strip('"') for g in dig(rec["type"], record_fqdn(rec.get("name"), zone))]
    want = str(rec.get("value") or "").lower().rstrip(".").strip('"')
    if rec["type"] == "MX":
        return any(g.split()[-1] == want for g in got if g.split())
    if rec["type"] == "TXT":
        return any(want.replace(" ", "") in g.replace('" "', "").replace(" ", "") for g in got)
    return want in got


def print_records(records, zone, where):
    say(f"\nDNS records for {where} (zone {zone}; the name is what goes in the Host box):")
    for r in records:
        prio = f"  priority {r['priority']}" if r.get("priority") is not None else ""
        say(f"  {r['type']:<6} {record_relative(record_fqdn(r.get('name'), zone), zone):<30} {r.get('value')}{prio}")


def resend_verify(dom, seconds=None):
    """Ask Resend to verify, then poll. True once the domain is verified."""
    seconds = int(os.environ.get("SITE_MAIL_VERIFY_SECONDS", "180")) if seconds is None else seconds
    resend("POST", f"/domains/{dom['id']}/verify", {}, ok=(200, 201, 202))
    deadline = time.time() + seconds
    while True:
        _, cur = resend("GET", f"/domains/{dom['id']}")
        if cur.get("status") == "verified":
            return True
        if time.time() >= deadline:
            say(f"  Resend says {dom['name']} is {cur.get('status')}: "
                + ", ".join(f"{r.get('record')} {r.get('status')}" for r in cur.get("records") or []))
            return False
        time.sleep(min(10, max(1, seconds // 6)))


def cf_zone_call(method, path, body=None):
    """One Cloudflare call outside /accounts (zones, DNS). (success, result, errors)."""
    tok, _ = cf_creds()
    data = json.dumps(body).encode() if body is not None else None
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{CF_API}{path}", data=data, method=method,
                                 headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {tok}", "Content-Type": "application/json",
                                          "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            payload = json.loads(r.read().decode())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        try:
            payload = json.loads(exc.read().decode())
        except ValueError:
            payload = {"success": False, "errors": [{"code": exc.code, "message": f"HTTP {exc.code}"}]}
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
        die(f"Cloudflare {method} {path}: {exc}")
    return bool(payload.get("success")), payload.get("result"), payload.get("errors") or []


def cf_zone(domain):
    """Our Cloudflare zone for `domain`, or die with a plain sentence when the token can't see one."""
    _, acct = cf_creds()
    ok, zones, errs = cf_zone_call("GET", f"/zones?name={domain}&account.id={acct}")
    if ok and zones:
        return zones[0]
    ok_all, seen, _ = cf_zone_call("GET", f"/zones?account.id={acct}&per_page=50")
    names = ", ".join(z["name"] for z in (seen or [])) if ok_all else "none it will list"
    die(f"{domain} isn't a zone our Cloudflare token can see (it sees: {names or 'none'}), so its records can't be "
        f"written from here. A domain whose DNS is elsewhere keeps its own mail: the owner uses the forward "
        f"(PLAYBOOK § Email). Nothing was changed.")


def cf_dns_records(zone_id, name, rtype=None):
    q = f"/zones/{zone_id}/dns_records?name={name}" + (f"&type={rtype}" if rtype else "")
    ok, rows, errs = cf_zone_call("GET", q)
    if not ok:
        die(f"Cloudflare won't list {name}'s records: " + "; ".join(f"{e.get('code')}: {e.get('message')}" for e in errs))
    return rows or []


def cf_write_record(zone, rec):
    """Write one Resend record into our zone unless it's already there. Returns what it did."""
    fqdn = record_fqdn(rec.get("name"), zone["name"])
    rtype = rec["type"]
    value = str(rec.get("value") or "")
    have = cf_dns_records(zone["id"], fqdn, rtype)
    norm = lambda s: str(s or "").lower().rstrip(".").strip('"')
    if any(norm(h.get("content")) == norm(value) for h in have):
        return f"{rtype} {fqdn} already there"
    if rtype == "CNAME" and have:
        die(f"{fqdn} already has a CNAME to {have[0].get('content')}; Resend wants {value}. Nothing more was written.")
    body = {"type": rtype, "name": fqdn, "content": value, "ttl": 1}
    if rtype == "MX":
        body["priority"] = int(rec.get("priority") or 10)
    if rtype == "CNAME":
        body["proxied"] = False
    if DRY:
        say(f"  would write {rtype} {fqdn} -> {value}" + (f" (priority {body['priority']})" if rtype == "MX" else ""))
        return f"{rtype} {fqdn} (dry run)"
    ok, _, errs = cf_zone_call("POST", f"/zones/{zone['id']}/dns_records", body)
    if not ok:
        die(f"Cloudflare refused {rtype} {fqdn}: " + "; ".join(f"{e.get('code')}: {e.get('message')}" for e in errs)
            + " (the token needs Zone · DNS · Edit on this zone)")
    return f"{rtype} {fqdn} written"


def mail_domain_setup(slug, domain, check=False):
    """--domain D: hello@D for a zone on our account whose apex has no mail. Resend domain
    with receiving on, its records into the zone, verify, then the mailbox PUT. Returns
    the address once it's live, or None."""
    require_admin("mail --domain")
    domain = re.sub(r"^https?://", "", domain.lower().strip().rstrip("/"))
    if domain.startswith("www."):
        domain = domain[4:]
    if not DOMAIN_RE.match(domain) or domain.count(".") != 1:
        die(f"{domain!r} isn't a bare domain (example.com); the address is hello@ the apex")
    zone = cf_zone(domain)
    existing = resend_domain(domain)                 # a re-run: Resend's own receiving MX isn't "their mail"
    ours = {str(r.get("value") or "").lower().rstrip(".") for r in (existing or {}).get("records") or [] if r.get("type") == "MX"}
    mx = [str(r.get("content") or "") for r in cf_dns_records(zone["id"], domain, "MX")] or dig("MX", domain)
    mx = [m for m in mx if m.split() and m.split()[-1].lower().rstrip(".") not in ours]
    if mx:
        die(f"{domain} already has mail (MX at the apex): they have mail there — the forward. "
            f"Their inbox stays where it is; PLAYBOOK § Email has the four Gmail steps. Nothing was changed.")
    address = f"hello@{domain}"
    say(f"mail for {slug}: {address} on {domain} (Cloudflare zone {zone['name']}, no mail at the apex)")
    if check:
        dom = resend_domain(domain)
        if not dom:
            say(f"  Resend has no domain {domain} yet (SITE_ADMIN=1 site mail --domain {domain} makes it)")
            return None
        say(f"  Resend: {dom.get('status')}, receiving {(dom.get('capabilities') or {}).get('receiving')}")
        for r in dom.get("records") or []:
            say(f"  {r.get('record', r['type']):<10} {r['type']:<6} {record_fqdn(r.get('name'), domain):<40} "
                f"{'ok' if dns_matches(r, domain) else 'not in DNS yet'} (Resend: {r.get('status')})")
        return address if dom.get("status") == "verified" else None
    dom = resend_ensure_domain(domain)
    if dom is None:                                    # dry run, domain not made
        say(f"  would write Resend's records into the {domain} zone, verify, then "
            f"PUT {json.dumps({'address': address, 'kind': 'domain', 'domains': [domain]})}")
        return address
    for rec in dom.get("records") or []:
        say("  " + cf_write_record(zone, rec))
    if DRY:
        mailbox_put(slug, {"address": address, "kind": "domain", "domains": [domain]})
        return address
    if not resend_verify(dom):
        say(f"  not verified yet; DNS can take a few minutes. Run this again (nothing is written twice): "
            f"SITE_ADMIN=1 site mail --domain {domain}")
        return None
    say(f"  Resend verified {domain}")
    mailbox_put(slug, {"address": address, "kind": "domain", "domains": [domain]})
    say(f"  patchlamp.com: {slug}'s mailbox is {address}")
    return address


def cmd_mail(a):
    """The site's address (plan 34): the mailbox on patchlamp.com and the Contact links
    that show it."""
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    if a.name == "platform":
        return mail_platform(a)
    if a.name == "doctor":
        sys.exit(0 if mail_doctor(say, lambda m: say(f"  FAIL {m}"), strict=True) else 1)
    ws, meta = workspace()
    slug = meta["slug"]
    reg = registry_load().get(slug, {})
    names = [a.name] if a.name else [n for n in repos_of(ws) if (reg.get(n) or {}).get("host") == "cloudflare"]
    for n in names:
        repo_dir(ws, n)
    if a.domain:
        address = mail_domain_setup(slug, a.domain, check=a.check)
        if a.check:
            say(f"  {address} is verified; the same command without --check sets the mailbox and the Contact links"
                if address else "  not live yet")
            sys.exit(0 if address else 1)
        if not address:
            sys.exit(1)
    else:
        box = mailbox_get(slug)
        address = box.get("address")
        if not address:
            address = mail_default(slug)
            say(f"  patchlamp.com has no mailbox for {slug}; {'would give' if DRY or a.check else 'giving'} it {address}")
            if not a.check:
                mailbox_put(slug, {"address": address, "kind": "platform"})
        else:
            say(f"mail for {slug}: {address} ({box.get('kind') or '?'}, {box.get('status') or '?'}, "
                f"replies go by {box.get('send_via') or 'resend'}{', answers by itself' if box.get('auto_reply') else ''})")
    behind = False
    if not names:
        say("  no Cloudflare site here to show it on (site new makes one; its Contact block carries the address)")
    for n in names:
        d = ws / "repos" / n
        links = mail_links(d)
        if not links:
            say(f"  repos/{n}: no data-mail link in its pages (a site made before B75). Add "
                f"<a data-mail href=\"mailto:{address}\">{address}</a> to its Contact block, commit, push, then site mail {n}")
            continue
        wrong = {rel: [mail_link_address(l) for l in ls] for rel, ls in links.items()
                 if any(mail_link_address(l) != address for l in ls)}
        if not wrong:
            say(f"  repos/{n}: the Contact links already say {address}")
            continue
        behind = True
        say(f"  repos/{n}: {', '.join(f'{rel} says {sorted(set(x))[0] or (chr(34) * 2)}' for rel, x in wrong.items())}")
        if a.check:
            continue
        _, dirty = git(d, "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=no", check=False)
        if dirty.strip():
            die(f"repos/{n} has uncommitted changes; commit them first, then site mail {n}")
        changed = rewrite_mail(d, address)
        say(f"  repos/{n}: {'would point' if DRY else 'pointed'} {len(changed)} page(s) at {address}: {', '.join(changed)}")
        git(d, "add", "--", *changed)
        git(d, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
            "commit", "-q", "-m", f"Contact: {address}")
        git(d, "push", "-q")
        cmd_publish(argparse.Namespace(name=n, dry_run=DRY))
    if DRY:
        say("dry run: nothing changed")
    if a.check and behind:
        sys.exit(1)


def mail_platform(a):
    """SITE_ADMIN: the Resend domain mail.patchlamp.com (sending + receiving) and the
    exact records for Porkbun, where patchlamp.com's DNS is (we have no Porkbun key).
    --check: public DNS (dig -4) against each record, then Resend's verify."""
    require_admin("mail platform")
    if a.check:
        dom = resend_domain(MAIL_DOMAIN)
        if not dom:
            say(f"{MAIL_DOMAIN}: not in Resend yet (SITE_ADMIN=1 site mail platform makes it)")
            sys.exit(1)
        missing = 0
        say(f"{MAIL_DOMAIN}: Resend {dom.get('status')}, receiving {(dom.get('capabilities') or {}).get('receiving')}")
        for r in dom.get("records") or []:
            ok_ = dns_matches(r, MAIL_ZONE)
            missing += not ok_
            say(f"  {r.get('record', r['type']):<10} {r['type']:<6} {record_fqdn(r.get('name'), MAIL_ZONE):<40} "
                f"{'in DNS' if ok_ else 'NOT in DNS yet'} (Resend: {r.get('status')})")
        if missing:
            say(f"{missing} record(s) not answering yet: paste them at Porkbun (site mail platform prints them); "
                f"DNS can take minutes")
            sys.exit(1)
        verified = dom.get("status") == "verified" or (not DRY and resend_verify(dom, seconds=30))
        say(f"{MAIL_DOMAIN}: {'verified: mail to <slug>@' + MAIL_DOMAIN + ' reaches Resend' if verified else 'records answer, Resend has not verified yet (again in a few minutes)'}")
        sys.exit(0 if verified else 1)
    dom = resend_ensure_domain(MAIL_DOMAIN)
    if dom is None:
        say(f"dry run: nothing created. Without --dry-run this makes the Resend domain {MAIL_DOMAIN} "
            f"and prints the records to paste at Porkbun.")
        return
    print_records(dom.get("records") or [], MAIL_ZONE, f"{MAIL_DOMAIN}, to paste at Porkbun → patchlamp.com → DNS")
    say("\nLeave the apex MX (Zoho, patchlamp.com's own inbox) as it is: these are all under mail. "
        "Then: SITE_ADMIN=1 site mail platform --check")


def mail_doctor(say_, fail_, strict=False):
    """The mail lines: the app's /internal/relay/mail/status, the platform domain's DNS,
    and, inside a workspace, the mailbox against the Contact links. `strict` (site mail
    doctor): not-ready is a failure; in `site doctor` it is a note until the app ships."""
    ok = True

    def bad(msg):
        nonlocal ok
        ok = False
        fail_(msg.strip())

    note = bad if strict else (lambda m: say_(f"  note: {m.strip()}"))
    say_("== mail (B75)")
    status = None
    try:
        code, status = app_call("GET", "/internal/relay/mail/status")
        if code != 200:
            bad(f"patchlamp.com mail status: HTTP {code}: {status.get('error')}")
            status = None
    except AppMissing:
        note(MAIL_NOT_YET)
    except SystemExit:
        bad("patchlamp.com's mail status couldn't be read (the line above says why)")
    if status:
        rk = str(status.get("resend_key") or "?")
        (say_ if rk == "ok" else bad)(f"  app: resend key {rk}")
        (say_ if status.get("webhook_secret") else note)("  app: webhook secret " + ("set" if status.get("webhook_secret")
                                                         else "MISSING (RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET in Laravel Cloud)"))
        (say_ if status.get("receiving") else note)(f"  app: receiving on {status.get('mail_domain') or MAIL_DOMAIN}: "
                                                    + ("yes" if status.get("receiving") else "not yet (site mail platform)"))
        say_(f"  app: gmail.send scope {'configured' if status.get('gmail_send_scope') else 'not configured'}; "
             f"{status.get('mailboxes', 0)} mailbox(es), {status.get('pending', 0)} mail(s) pending")
    mx = dig("MX", MAIL_DOMAIN)
    (say_ if mx else note)(f"  DNS: MX {MAIL_DOMAIN} " + (", ".join(mx) if mx else "none yet (SITE_ADMIN=1 site mail platform)"))
    if (Path.cwd() / ".client.json").exists() and status is not None:
        ws, meta = workspace()
        try:
            code, data = app_call("GET", f"/internal/relay/projects/{meta['slug']}/mailbox")
            box = (data.get("mailbox") or {}) if code == 200 else {}
        except AppMissing:
            box = None
        if box is None:
            note(MAIL_NOT_YET)
        elif not box.get("address"):
            note(f"{meta['slug']} has no mailbox on patchlamp.com (site mail gives it {mail_default(meta['slug'])})")
        else:
            say_(f"  mailbox: {box['address']} ({box.get('status')}, replies by {box.get('send_via') or 'resend'})")
            for n in repos_of(ws):
                links = mail_links(ws / "repos" / n)
                addrs = sorted({mail_link_address(l) for ls in links.values() for l in ls})
                if not links:
                    say_(f"  repos/{n}: no data-mail link (site mail {n} says how to add one)")
                elif addrs != [box["address"]]:
                    bad(f"repos/{n}: the Contact links say {', '.join(addrs)}, the mailbox is {box['address']} (site mail {n})")
                else:
                    say_(f"  repos/{n}: the Contact links say {box['address']}")
    return ok


def cmd_adopt(a):
    """Register an existing repo (made for GitHub Pages) as a Cloudflare site
    and create its project. Doesn't touch DNS or GitHub Pages: publish, look,
    `site domain`, and only then flip the records."""
    require_admin("adopt")
    global DRY
    DRY = a.dry_run
    ws, meta = workspace()
    d = repo_dir(ws, a.name)
    project = a.project or a.name
    if not NAME_RE.match(project) or len(project) > 58:
        die(f"{project!r} isn't a valid Pages project name")
    existing = site_entry(meta, a.name)
    if existing and existing.get("project") not in (None, project):
        die(f"repos/{a.name} is already registered as project {existing['project']}")
    for slug, repos in registry_load().items():
        for rname, row in repos.items():
            if row.get("project") == project and (slug, rname) != (meta["slug"], a.name):
                die(f"project {project} already belongs to {slug}/{rname}")
    cf_ensure_project(project)
    row = site_register(meta, a.name, project)
    say(f"registered {meta['slug']}/{a.name} -> Cloudflare Pages project {project} ({REGISTRY})")
    say(f"next: site publish {a.name}; then SITE_ADMIN=1 site domain {a.name} <domain>")


def cmd_stamp(a):
    """Stamp a new build id into version.json, every page's freshness check
    and the css/js cache-busters — the body of the site's own tools/stamp,
    run from the toolbelt so a client session can use it without an allow
    rule for an in-repo script (which the session could rewrite). Workspace-
    only, and the repo must be one of ./repos/*; no other path is touched."""
    import re
    from datetime import datetime, timezone
    ws, _ = workspace()
    name = Path(a.name).name                         # "repos/x", "x/", "../x" all collapse to "x"
    d = (ws / "repos" / name).resolve()
    if not d.is_dir() or (ws / "repos").resolve() not in d.parents:
        die(f"{a.name!r} is not a repo under ./repos (site ls shows them)")
    if not (d / ".git").exists():
        die(f"repos/{name} is not a git repo")
    pages = sorted(d.glob("*.html"))
    if not pages:
        die(f"repos/{name} has no *.html at its root; nothing to stamp")
    build = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
    (d / "version.json").write_text('{"build": "%s"}\n' % build)
    touched = 0
    for page in pages:
        text = page.read_text()
        new = re.sub(r'var BUILD = "[^"]*";', f'var BUILD = "{build}";', text)
        new = re.sub(r'css/style\.css\?v=[^"]*', f'css/style.css?v={build}', new)
        new = re.sub(r'js/main\.js\?v=[^"]*', f'js/main.js?v={build}', new)
        if new != text:
            page.write_text(new)
            touched += 1
    say(f"stamped build {build} into repos/{name}: version.json + {touched} of {len(pages)} pages")
    if a.commit:
        subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(d), "add", "-A"], check=True)
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(d), "commit", "-m", a.commit], capture_output=True, text=True)
        say(r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[0] if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip() else (r.stderr.strip() or "nothing to commit"))


def cmd_ls(a):
    ws, meta = workspace()
    names = repos_of(ws)
    if not names:
        say("no repos in ./repos yet (site new <name>)")
        return
    for n in names:
        d = ws / "repos" / n
        slug = remote_slug(d) or "-"
        entry = site_entry(meta, n)
        if entry and entry.get("host") == "cloudflare":
            proj = entry["project"]
            live = f"https://{entry['domains'][0]}/" if entry.get("domains") else f"https://{pages_host(proj)}/"
            extra = [f"cloudflare:{proj}"] + [f"domain={x}" for x in entry.get("domains") or []]
            same = lambda u: re.sub(r"^https?://", "", (u or "").rstrip("/"))
            star = " *" if meta.get("live_url") and same(live) == same(meta["live_url"]) else ""
            say(f"{n:<24} {slug:<32} {live}{star}  {' '.join(extra)}")
            continue
        info = pages_info(slug) if slug != "-" else None
        if info:
            live = info.get("html_url") or "-"
            extra = []
            if info.get("cname"):
                extra.append(f"domain={info['cname']}" + (" https" if info.get("https_enforced") else " http-only"))
            if info.get("status") and info["status"] != "built":
                extra.append(f"status={info['status']}")
        else:
            live, extra = "(Pages off or no access)", []
        same = lambda u: re.sub(r"^https?://", "", (u or "").rstrip("/"))
        star = " *" if meta.get("live_url") and same(live) == same(meta["live_url"]) else ""
        say(f"{n:<24} {slug:<32} {live}{star}  {' '.join(extra)}")
    if meta.get("live_url"):
        say(f"\n* = live_url in .client.json (the URL the allowlist can curl): {meta['live_url']}")


def cf_domain(ws, meta, d, name, entry, a):
    """Custom domain for a Cloudflare site: apex + www on the Pages project,
    canonical links in the repo, and the two records for the registrar.
    Cloudflare validates once the records resolve and issues the certificate
    itself; `site domain <name>` (no domain) shows where that's at."""
    project = entry["project"]
    if not a.domain:
        doms = cf_domains(project)
        say(f"{name}: Pages project {project} -> https://{project}.pages.dev/")
        if not doms:
            say("  custom domains: (none)")
        for dm in doms:
            cert = (dm.get("certificate_authority") or "") and dm.get("status")
            say(f"  {dm['name']:<32} domain {dm.get('status')}, validation {dm.get('validation_data', {}).get('status', '-')}, "
                f"certificate {dm.get('certificate_authority') or '-'}")
        return
    domain = re.sub(r"^https?://", "", a.domain.lower().strip().rstrip("/"))
    if not DOMAIN_RE.match(domain):
        die(f"{domain!r} doesn't look like a domain")
    apex = domain.count(".") == 1
    wanted = [domain, f"www.{domain}"] if apex else [domain]
    have = {dm["name"] for dm in cf_domains(project)}
    for dm in wanted:
        if dm in have:
            say(f"  {dm} already on {project}")
        else:
            cf_api("POST", f"/pages/projects/{project}/domains", {"name": dm})
            say(f"  added {dm} to {project}")
    new_url = f"https://{domain}/"

    # the repo: canonical links to the bare domain (Pages can't redirect one
    # host to another from _redirects, so www serves the same site), and the
    # live URL in the manual/allowlist
    changed = []
    if apex:
        for page in sorted(d.glob("*.html")):
            text = page.read_text()
            if 'rel="canonical"' in text or page.name == "404.html" or "<head>" not in text:
                continue
            path = "" if page.name == "index.html" else page.name[:-5]
            text = text.replace("<head>", f'<head>\n  <link rel="canonical" href="{new_url}{path}">', 1)
            page.write_text(text)
            changed.append(page.name)
    old_url = meta.get("live_url") or f"https://{pages_host(project)}/"
    for f in FILLED_FILES:
        p = d / f
        if p.exists() and old_url in p.read_text() and old_url != new_url:
            p.write_text(p.read_text().replace(old_url, new_url))
            changed.append(f)
    if changed and not DRY:
        git(d, "add", *changed)
        git(d, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
            "commit", "-q", "-m", f"Point the site at {domain}")
        git(d, "push", "-q")
        say(f"  committed {', '.join(changed)} and pushed")

    site_register(meta, name, project, wanted)
    set_live_url(ws, meta, new_url, force=True)
    restamp(ws, meta)
    if changed and not DRY:
        cmd_publish(argparse.Namespace(name=name, dry_run=False))

    target = pages_host(project)
    say(f"\nDNS records at the registrar for {domain} (replace any A/CNAME already there for these names):")
    if apex:
        say(f"  ALIAS  @      {target}     (Porkbun: ALIAS; elsewhere ANAME/'CNAME flattening'; "
            f"if the registrar can't, move the nameservers to Cloudflare)")
        say(f"  CNAME  www    {target}")
    else:
        say(f"  CNAME  {domain.split('.', 1)[0]:<6} {target}")
    say(f"\nCloudflare checks the records itself (minutes once DNS has propagated), then issues the "
        f"certificate; `SITE_ADMIN=1 site domain {name}` shows the state. Live URL is now {new_url}."
        + (f"\nwww.{domain} serves the same site (Pages can't redirect hosts); every page now carries a "
           f"canonical link to {new_url}, which is what search engines go by." if apex else ""))


def cmd_domain(a):
    require_admin("domain")
    ws, meta = workspace()
    d = repo_dir(ws, a.name)
    entry = site_entry(meta, a.name)
    if entry and entry.get("host") == "cloudflare":
        cf_domain(ws, meta, d, a.name, entry, a)
        return
    slug = remote_slug(d)
    if not slug:
        die(f"repos/{a.name} has no GitHub remote")
    o = slug.split("/")[0]
    if not a.domain:
        info = pages_info(slug)
        if not info:
            die(f"Pages is not enabled for {slug}")
        say(f"{slug}: {info.get('html_url')}")
        say(f"  custom domain: {info.get('cname') or '(none)'}")
        say(f"  https enforced: {info.get('https_enforced')}")
        say(f"  domain state: {info.get('protected_domain_state') or '-'}, build status: {info.get('status')}")
        if a.https:
            gh("api", "-X", "PUT", f"repos/{slug}/pages", "--input", "-", stdin=json.dumps({"https_enforced": True}))
            say("  https enforced: True (set now)")
        return
    domain = a.domain.lower().strip().rstrip("/")
    domain = re.sub(r"^https?://", "", domain)
    if not DOMAIN_RE.match(domain):
        die(f"{domain!r} doesn't look like a domain")
    old_info = pages_info(slug) or {}
    old_url = (old_info.get("html_url") or pages_url(o, a.name)).rstrip("/") + "/"
    new_url = f"https://{domain}/"

    # the repo: CNAME + the live URL in the manual/allowlist
    (d / "CNAME").write_text(domain + "\n")
    for f in FILLED_FILES:
        p = d / f
        if p.exists() and old_url in p.read_text():
            p.write_text(p.read_text().replace(old_url, new_url))
    git(d, "add", "CNAME", *[f for f in FILLED_FILES if (d / f).exists()])
    code, status = git(d, "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=no", check=False)
    if status.strip():
        git(d, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
            "commit", "-q", "-m", f"Point the site at {domain}")
        git(d, "push", "-q")
        say(f"  committed CNAME and pushed")

    # GitHub Pages
    gh("api", "-X", "PUT", f"repos/{slug}/pages", "--input", "-", stdin=json.dumps({"cname": domain}))
    say(f"  Pages custom domain set to {domain}")
    if a.https:
        code, out, err = gh("api", "-X", "PUT", f"repos/{slug}/pages", "--input", "-",
                            stdin=json.dumps({"https_enforced": True}), check=False)
        say("  https enforced" if code == 0 else
            f"  https not enforced yet ({(err or out).splitlines()[-1] if (err or out) else 'certificate pending'}); "
            f"re-run `SITE_ADMIN=1 site domain {a.name} --https` once DNS has propagated")

    # the workspace
    set_live_url(ws, meta, new_url, force=True)
    restamp(ws, meta)

    # what to tell the registrar
    apex = domain if domain.count(".") == 1 else None
    target = f"{o.lower()}.github.io"
    say(f"\nDNS records to add at the registrar for {domain}:")
    if apex:
        for ip in PAGES_IPS:
            say(f"  A      @      {ip}")
        say(f"  CNAME  www    {target}")
    else:
        sub = domain.split(".", 1)[0]
        say(f"  CNAME  {sub:<6} {target}")
        say(f"  (and, if the bare domain should redirect here, A records for @ → {', '.join(PAGES_IPS)})")
    say(f"\nThen: wait for DNS (minutes to a day), `SITE_ADMIN=1 site domain {a.name}` shows the state, "
        f"and `--https` turns on Enforce HTTPS once GitHub has the certificate. Live URL is now {new_url}.")


def cmd_transfer(a):
    require_admin("transfer")
    ws, meta = workspace()
    d = repo_dir(ws, a.name)
    slug = remote_slug(d)
    if not slug:
        die(f"repos/{a.name} has no GitHub remote")
    if not re.match(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]{0,38}$", a.user):
        die(f"{a.user!r} is not a valid GitHub user/org name")
    if not gh_json("api", f"users/{a.user}"):
        die(f"GitHub has no account named {a.user}")
    _, dirty = git(d, "status", "--porcelain", check=False)
    _, unpushed = git(d, "log", "--oneline", "@{u}..", check=False)
    if dirty.strip() or unpushed.strip():
        die(f"repos/{a.name} has {'uncommitted changes' if dirty.strip() else 'unpushed commits'}; "
            f"commit and push first so the client gets everything")
    info = pages_info(slug) or {}
    code, out, err = gh("api", "-X", "POST", f"repos/{slug}/transfer", "--input", "-",
                        stdin=json.dumps({"new_owner": a.user}), check=False)
    if code != 0:
        die(f"transfer refused: {err or out}")
    name = slug.split("/")[1]
    say(f"transfer of {slug} to {a.user} requested.")
    say(f"  GitHub emails {a.user}; they accept within 24 hours, then the repo is https://github.com/{a.user}/{name}")
    say(f"  Pages will publish at https://{a.user.lower()}.github.io/{name}/ from their Settings → Pages (main, root)"
        + (f"; their custom domain {info['cname']} keeps working once DNS `www` (or the subdomain) points at "
           f"{a.user.lower()}.github.io — the A records don't change" if info.get("cname") else ""))
    say(f"  we lose write access when they accept, so this workspace stops managing it.")
    old_url = (info.get("html_url") or "").rstrip("/") + "/" if info.get("html_url") else None
    if meta.get("live_url") and old_url and meta["live_url"].rstrip("/") + "/" == old_url:
        meta["live_url"] = None
        write_meta(ws, meta)
        restamp(ws, meta)
    if a.keep:
        say(f"  repos/{a.name} kept (--keep); remove it once they've accepted")
    else:
        shutil.rmtree(d)
        say(f"  removed repos/{a.name} from the workspace (everything is on GitHub; the relay no longer sees it)")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- handover (B69)
# Leaving Patchlamp in an hour (VISION § Decided 2026-09-29): one command puts
# everything that is the client's into handover/<date>/ and one zip beside it,
# uploads the zip to their account page, and prints its path last for SEND-FILE.

CHATS_BIN = HERE / "bin" / "chats"
RELAY_DIR = Path(os.environ.get("RELAY_DIR", Path.home() / "projects" / "sms-relay"))
HANDOVER_DIR = "handover"                          # in the workspace; ignores itself (handover/.gitignore)
HANDOVER_MAX_BYTES = 20 * 1024 * 1024              # what patchlamp.com's account page takes (its chat-media cap)


def is_demo(slug):
    """The six template demos (as `demo` knows them): strangers text these, so a
    demo's handover carries only the asker's own conversation."""
    return slug == "testaurant" or slug.startswith("demo-")


def handover_run(cmd, cwd, timeout=300):
    """(code, stdout, stderr) of a sibling tool; never raises."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([str(c) for c in cmd], cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)
        return r.returncode, r.stdout, r.stderr
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:
        return 1, "", str(exc)


def handover_repo(repo, out, name):
    """The site's files as a zip (opens anywhere) and its whole history as a git
    bundle (`git clone site-<name>.bundle`). Returns (lines, problems)."""
    lines, problems = [], []
    code, _, err = handover_run(["git", "-C", repo, "archive", "--format=zip", f"--prefix={name}/",
                                 "-o", out / f"site-{name}.zip", "HEAD"], out)
    if code:
        problems.append(f"repos/{name}: git archive failed: {err.strip()[:160]}")
    else:
        lines.append(f"site-{name}.zip — the site's files as they are published (HEAD)")
    code, _, err = handover_run(["git", "-C", repo, "bundle", "create", out / f"site-{name}.bundle", "--all"], out)
    if code:
        problems.append(f"repos/{name}: git bundle failed: {err.strip()[:160]}")
    else:
        lines.append(f"site-{name}.bundle — the same site with its whole history (`git clone site-{name}.bundle`)")
    code, dirty, _ = handover_run(["git", "-C", repo, "status", "--porcelain"], out)
    if code == 0 and dirty.strip():
        problems.append(f"repos/{name}: uncommitted changes are not in the bundle (commit them and run it again)")
    return lines, problems


def handover_database(ws, out, name, started):
    """`db export --site <name>`, copied into database/<name>/."""
    code, so, se = handover_run([DB_BIN, "export", "--site", name], ws)
    if code:
        return [], [f"{name}: db export failed: {(se or so).strip()[:200]}"]
    day = datetime.date.today().isoformat()
    src = ws / "exports" / day
    dest = out / "database" / name
    dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    n = 0
    for p in sorted(src.glob("*")) if src.is_dir() else []:
        if p.is_file() and p.stat().st_mtime >= started - 1:
            shutil.copy2(p, dest / p.name)
            n += 1
    if not n:
        return [f"database/{name}/ — empty: the database has no tables yet"], []
    return [f"database/{name}/ — every table as CSV and JSON ({n} file{'s' if n != 1 else ''})"], []


def handover_newsletter(ws, out):
    code, so, se = handover_run([NEWSLETTER_BIN, "subscribers", "--json"], ws, timeout=90)
    if code:
        why = (se or so).strip()
        if "isn't registered" in why or "newsletter setup" in why:
            return [], [], "no mailing list on patchlamp.com"
        return [], [f"newsletter: {why[:200]}"], ""
    try:
        subs = json.loads(so or "[]")
    except ValueError:
        return [], ["newsletter: the list didn't come back as JSON"], ""
    import csv
    cols = ["email"] + sorted({k for s in subs for k in s} - {"email"})
    with open(out / "newsletter-subscribers.csv", "w", newline="") as f:
        w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=cols, extrasaction="ignore")
        w.writeheader()
        w.writerows(subs)
    return [f"newsletter-subscribers.csv — your mailing list ({len(subs)} on it)"], [], ""


def handover_chats(ws, out, slug):
    cmd = [CHATS_BIN, "--project", slug, "-n", "0", "--out", out / "chats.html"]
    if is_demo(slug):
        who = os.environ.get("RELAY_SENDER_KEY", "")
        if not who:
            return [], [], "a demo: the conversation goes only to the person who had it (no RELAY_SENDER_KEY here)"
        cmd += ["--from", who]
    code, so, se = handover_run(cmd, ws, timeout=180)
    if code or not (out / "chats.html").is_file():
        return [], [f"chats: {(se or so).strip()[:200] or 'no page written'}"], ""
    return ["chats.html — every conversation with Patch, the photos inside it (opens in any browser)"], [], ""


def handover_schedules(out, slug):
    """What runs for them on its own (the list on /account): relay state, read only."""
    p = RELAY_DIR / "state" / "schedules.json"
    try:
        jobs = [j for j in json.loads(p.read_text()).get("jobs", [])
                if j.get("project") == slug and j.get("state") != "stopped"]
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        jobs = []
    keep = ("id", "human", "cron", "tz", "text", "kind", "state", "last_fired")
    rows = [{k: j.get(k) for k in keep if j.get(k) is not None} for j in jobs]
    (out / "schedules.json").write_text(json.dumps(rows, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
    return [f"schedules.json — what Patch runs for you on its own ({len(rows)} job{'s' if len(rows) != 1 else ''})"], rows


def handover_readme(ws, meta, repos, have, rows, notes, day):
    reg = registry_load().get(meta["slug"], {})
    L = [f"# {meta.get('name') or meta['slug']} — everything that's yours", "",
         f"Made {day} by Patch (`site handover`). Every file here opens without Patchlamp.", "",
         "## What's in here", ""]
    L += [f"- {h}" for h in have] + [""]
    if notes:
        L += ["Not included:", ""] + [f"- {n}" for n in notes] + [""]
    L += ["## What runs where", ""]
    for n in repos:
        e = reg.get(n) or {}
        L.append(f"### {n}")
        L.append("")
        if e.get("host") == "cloudflare":
            host = e.get("pages_host") or f"{e.get('project')}.pages.dev"
            L.append(f"- Served by Cloudflare Pages, project `{e.get('project')}`, at https://{host}/ .")
        else:
            L.append("- Served by GitHub Pages from its repository.")
        slug = remote_slug(ws / "repos" / n)
        if slug:
            L.append(f"- The repository is github.com/{slug}. On request it is transferred to a GitHub account you control.")
        for dm in e.get("domains") or []:
            L.append(f"- Your domain {dm} is registered in your name at your registrar; it points at Cloudflare today.")
        if (e.get("d1") or {}).get("name"):
            L.append(f"- Its database is Cloudflare D1 `{e['d1']['name']}`; the /admin page and the forms that save to it "
                     "run as Pages Functions (functions/ in the repo). On another host those parts need their own "
                     "backend; the data is in database/ as CSV and JSON.")
        L.append("")
    L += ["## Moving the site somewhere else", "",
          "1. Unzip `site-<name>.zip` and upload the files to any static host (Netlify, GitHub Pages, Cloudflare "
          "on your own account, your own server). There is no build step.",
          "2. At the registrar where you bought your domain, change its DNS records to the ones the new host gives you "
          "(usually one CNAME for www and one A or ALIAS record for the bare domain). Or tell Patch where it's going "
          "and Taylor points it for you.",
          "3. We keep serving the site at its current address for thirty days after the handover, so there is no gap.",
          ""]
    if rows:
        L += ["## What ran on its own", ""]
        L += [f"- {r.get('human') or r.get('cron')}: {r.get('text')}" for r in rows] + [""]
    L += ["## The rest", ""]
    if any(h.startswith("newsletter-subscribers.csv") for h in have):
        L.append("- The mailing list lived on patchlamp.com; it is newsletter-subscribers.csv, ready to import anywhere.")
    L.append("- If you took payments through Patch, that Stripe account is yours, in your name; nothing changes there.")
    if any(h.startswith("memory.md") for h in have):
        L.append("- memory.md is what Patch kept about your business; schedules.json is what ran for you. Together "
                 "they are your operating manual.")
    L.append("")
    return "\n".join(L)


def handover_zip(out, dest):
    import zipfile
    with zipfile.ZipFile(dest, "w", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:
        for p in sorted(out.rglob("*")):
            if p.is_file():
                z.write(p, f"{dest.stem}/{p.relative_to(out)}")
    return dest


def handover_upload(slug, path):
    """The zip to patchlamp.com, where the account page offers it behind the sign-in.
    Returns the line to print."""
    env = read_env()
    secret = os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET") or env.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET")
    base = (os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_URL") or env.get("PATCHLAMP_URL") or "https://patchlamp.com").rstrip("/")
    if not secret:
        return "account page: not uploaded (no PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET in the toolbelt)"
    size = path.stat().st_size
    if size > HANDOVER_MAX_BYTES:
        return (f"account page: not uploaded — {size / 1048576:.1f} MB is over the page's "
                f"{HANDOVER_MAX_BYTES // 1048576} MB; attach it here or FORWARD-TO-TAYLOR to send it")
    boundary = "----handover" + secrets.token_hex(12)
    body = b"".join([
        f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; filename=\"{path.name}\"\r\n"
        f"Content-Type: application/zip\r\n\r\n".encode(), path.read_bytes(), f"\r\n--{boundary}--\r\n".encode()])
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{base}/internal/relay/projects/{slug}/handover", data=body, method="POST", headers={
        "Authorization": f"Bearer {secret}", "Accept": "application/json",
        "Content-Type": f"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}", "User-Agent": "claude-tools site"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=120) as r:
            res = json.loads(r.read().decode() or "{}")
        return f"account page: uploaded — {res.get('account') or base + '/account'} (Your files)"
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
        return f"account page: not uploaded (HTTP {exc.code})"
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        return f"account page: not uploaded ({str(exc)[:120]})"


def cmd_handover(a):
    ws, meta = workspace()
    slug = meta["slug"]
    day = datetime.date.today().isoformat()
    root = ws / HANDOVER_DIR
    out = Path(a.out).expanduser() if a.out else root / day
    if not out.is_absolute():
        out = ws / out
    repos = [a.name] if a.name else repos_of(ws)
    for n in repos:
        repo_dir(ws, n)
    if a.dry_run:
        say(f"would build {out}/ from: {', '.join('repos/' + n for n in repos) or 'no repos'}, the database export, "
            f"the mailing list, the conversations, memory.md, the schedules, a README; zip beside it"
            + ("" if a.no_upload or is_demo(slug) else "; upload to the account page"))
        return
    root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (root / ".gitignore").write_text("# the client's own data: never in the clients/ repo\n*\n")
    if out.exists():
        shutil.rmtree(out)
    out.mkdir(parents=True)
    started = time.time()
    have, problems, notes = [], [], []
    for n in repos:
        h, p = handover_repo(ws / "repos" / n, out, n)
        have += h; problems += p
    if not repos:
        notes.append("no site repository in this workspace")
    reg = registry_load().get(slug, {})
    for n in repos:
        if (reg.get(n, {}).get("d1") or {}).get("name"):
            h, p = handover_database(ws, out, n, started)
            have += h; problems += p
    h, p, note = handover_newsletter(ws, out)
    have += h; problems += p
    if note:
        notes.append(note)
    h, p, note = handover_chats(ws, out, slug)
    have += h; problems += p
    if note:
        notes.append(note)
    rows = []
    if is_demo(slug):
        notes.append("memory.md and the schedules: a demo's are shared by everyone who texts it")
    else:
        if (ws / "memory.md").is_file():
            shutil.copy2(ws / "memory.md", out / "memory.md")
            have.append("memory.md — what Patch knows about your business")
        else:
            notes.append("memory.md: Patch hasn't written one for this business yet")
        h, rows = handover_schedules(out, slug)
        have += h
    have.append("README.md — this page: what runs where, and how to move it")
    (out / "README.md").write_text(handover_readme(ws, meta, repos, have, rows,
                                                   notes + [f"{p} (Patch has passed it on)" for p in problems], day))
    z = handover_zip(out, out.parent / f"{slug}-handover-{day}.zip")
    say(f"handover for {meta.get('name') or slug}: {out}/")
    for line in have:
        say(f"  {line}")
    for line in notes:
        say(f"  not included: {line}")
    for line in problems:
        say(f"  PROBLEM {line}")
    if a.no_upload or is_demo(slug):
        say("account page: not uploaded" + (" (a demo has no account page)" if is_demo(slug) else " (--no-upload)"))
    else:
        say(handover_upload(slug, z))
    say(f"{z.stat().st_size / 1048576:.1f} MB")
    print(z.resolve())                              # last, for SEND-FILE; PROBLEM lines above say what's missing


def handover_doctor(say_, fail_):
    """Can a handover be built here? (site doctor's own lines, B69)"""
    ws, meta = workspace()
    say_("== handover")
    for tool in (DB_BIN, NEWSLETTER_BIN, CHATS_BIN):
        (say_ if tool.exists() else fail_)(f"  {tool.name}: {'present' if tool.exists() else 'MISSING'}")
    if not shutil.which("git"):
        fail_("git is not installed")
    say_(f"  memory.md: {'present' if (ws / 'memory.md').is_file() else 'none yet'}")
    say_(f"  relay schedules: {'readable' if (RELAY_DIR / 'state' / 'schedules.json').is_file() else 'not found (the list comes out empty)'}")
    env = read_env()
    has = bool(os.environ.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET") or env.get("PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET"))
    say_(f"  account page upload: {'on' if has else 'off (no PATCHLAMP_RELAY_SHARED_SECRET)'}"
         + (" — a demo never uploads" if is_demo(meta['slug']) else ""))
    last = sorted((ws / HANDOVER_DIR).glob("*.zip")) if (ws / HANDOVER_DIR).is_dir() else []
    say_(f"  last handover: {last[-1].name if last else 'none'} (site handover builds one)")


def cmd_retire(a):
    """Take a site down for good: its Pages project (custom domains first), its
    registry row, the workspace's live_url if it was this site, the local
    clone. The GitHub repo stays — it is the record and what a client gets on
    exit — unless --delete-repo, which is for throwaway runs. Never touches
    config.json: the relay's project entry is the owner's to remove."""
    global DRY
    require_admin("retire")
    ws, meta = workspace()
    name = a.name
    if not NAME_RE.match(name):
        die(f"{name!r} is not a valid site name")
    d = ws / "repos" / name
    entry = site_entry(meta, name)
    slug = remote_slug(d) if d.is_dir() else None     # a read; before DRY so the dry run can name the repo
    DRY = a.dry_run
    if not entry and not d.is_dir():
        die(f"nothing to retire: repos/{name} is not here and the registry has no {meta['slug']}/{name}")
    project = (entry or {}).get("project") or name
    say(f"site retire {name} for {meta['name']} ({meta['slug']}){' — DRY RUN' if DRY else ''}")

    # 1. the host: domains, then the project
    if entry and entry.get("host") == "cloudflare":
        cf_creds()
        if cf_project(project):
            for dom in cf_domains(project):
                cf_api("DELETE", f"/pages/projects/{project}/domains/{dom['name']}", ok404=True)
                say(f"  detached {dom['name']} (the DNS records at the registrar are still theirs to remove)")
            cf_api("DELETE", f"/pages/projects/{project}", ok404=True)
            say(f"  deleted Pages project {project} (https://{project}.pages.dev is gone)")
        else:
            say(f"  Pages project {project} was already gone")
    elif entry:
        say(f"  registry says host {entry.get('host')!r}; nothing to delete on a host")
    else:
        say("  not in the registry (GitHub Pages era or never adopted); host untouched")

    # 2. the registry
    if entry:
        reg = registry_load()
        reg.get(meta["slug"], {}).pop(name, None)
        if not reg.get(meta["slug"]):
            reg.pop(meta["slug"], None)
        if not DRY:
            registry_save(reg)
        say(f"  removed {meta['slug']}/{name} from the registry")

    # 3. the repo on GitHub
    if slug:
        if a.delete_repo:
            code, out, err = gh("repo", "delete", slug, "--yes", check=False) if not DRY else (0, "", "")
            if code == 0:
                say(f"  deleted https://github.com/{slug}" + (" (dry run)" if DRY else ""))
            else:
                say(f"  WARN could not delete {slug}: {(err or out).strip()[:200]}. Delete it on GitHub "
                    f"(the token needs Administration: write) or leave it")
        else:
            say(f"  kept https://github.com/{slug} (the record; --delete-repo removes it, `site transfer` hands it over)")

    # 4. the workspace
    url = f"https://{pages_host(project)}/"
    if meta.get("live_url") and meta["live_url"].rstrip("/") + "/" == url:
        meta["live_url"] = None
        if not DRY:
            write_meta(ws, meta)
            restamp(ws, meta)
        say("  live_url cleared (the workspace no longer points at it)")
    if d.is_dir():
        if a.keep_local:
            say(f"  repos/{name} kept (--keep-local)")
        else:
            if not DRY:
                shutil.rmtree(d)
            say(f"  removed repos/{name}")
    say()
    say(f"retired {name}." + (" Nothing changed (dry run)." if DRY else "")
        + f" If the relay has a project for {meta['slug']}, remove or pause it in config.json.")


def cmd_template(a):
    if a.action != "push":
        die("site template push is the only template action")
    o = owner()
    kind = a.template or DEFAULT_TEMPLATE
    use_template(kind)
    slug = f"{o}/{template_repo()}" + ("" if kind == DEFAULT_TEMPLATE else f"-{kind}")
    _, sha = git(HERE, "rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD", check=False)
    code, _, _ = gh("repo", "view", slug, "--json", "name", check=False)
    if code != 0:
        gh("repo", "create", slug, "--public", "--disable-wiki", "--disable-issues",
           "--description", "Template for client sites made by `site new` (claude-tools)")
        say(f"  created https://github.com/{slug}")
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="site-template-") as tmp:
        work = Path(tmp) / "repo"
        code, _, err = gh("repo", "clone", slug, str(work), "--", "-q", check=False)
        if code != 0:
            die(f"clone failed: {err}")
        for p in list(work.iterdir()):
            if p.name != ".git":
                shutil.rmtree(p) if p.is_dir() else p.unlink()
        shutil.copytree(TEMPLATE_DIR, work, dirs_exist_ok=True, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(TEMPLATE_META))
        (work / "TEMPLATE.md").write_text(
            f"# site-template\n\nThe files `site new` copies for a new client site, mirrored from "
            f"`claude-tools/templates/sites/{kind}/` (commit {sha or '?'}). The `{{{{NAME}}}}`-style placeholders are "
            f"filled at creation; edit the source in claude-tools, then `site template push`.\n")
        git(work, "add", "-A")
        _, status = git(work, "status", "--porcelain", check=False)
        if not status.strip():
            say(f"{slug} already matches templates/sites/{kind}")
        else:
            _, branch = git(work, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "HEAD", check=False)
            git(work, "-c", "user.name=Patch (claude-tools site)", "-c", "user.email=noreply@anthropic.com",
                "commit", "-q", "-m", f"Sync from claude-tools templates/sites/{kind} ({sha or 'local'})")
            git(work, "push", "-q", "-u", "origin", branch if branch not in ("", "HEAD") else "main")
            say(f"  pushed templates/sites/{kind} to {slug}")
    gh("api", "-X", "PATCH", f"repos/{slug}", "--input", "-", stdin=json.dumps({"is_template": True}))
    say(f"  https://github.com/{slug} is a template repo")


def cmd_doctor(a):
    ok = True

    def fail(msg):
        nonlocal ok
        ok = False
        say(f"  FAIL {msg}")

    say("== auth")
    src, _ = token_source()
    say(f"  token: {src}")
    if not shutil.which("gh"):
        fail("gh is not installed")
    else:
        code, login, err = gh("api", "user", "--jq", ".login", check=False)
        if code == 0:
            say(f"  gh authenticates as {login}")
        else:
            fail(f"gh cannot authenticate: {err.splitlines()[-1] if err else 'unknown'} (gh auth login, or setenv.sh GITHUB_TOKEN)")
    say("== owner")
    o = os.environ.get("SITE_ORG") or read_env().get("SITE_ORG")
    if not o:
        fail("SITE_ORG unset (setenv.sh SITE_ORG once the org exists; TAYLOR-TODO §1)")
    else:
        kind = "org" if gh_json("api", f"orgs/{o}") else ("user" if gh_json("api", f"users/{o}") else None)
        if kind:
            say(f"  SITE_ORG={o} ({kind})")
            tslug = f"{o}/{template_repo()}"
            code, _, _ = gh("repo", "view", tslug, "--json", "name", check=False)
            say(f"  template mirror {tslug}: {'present' if code == 0 else 'absent (site template push)'}")
        else:
            fail(f"SITE_ORG={o} is not reachable on GitHub")
    say("== templates")
    kinds = templates()
    if DEFAULT_TEMPLATE not in kinds:
        fail(f"no {DEFAULT_TEMPLATE} template at {SITES_DIR / DEFAULT_TEMPLATE}")
    for kind in kinds:
        tdir = SITES_DIR / kind
        found = set()
        for p in tdir.rglob("*"):
            if p.is_file():
                try:
                    found |= set(re.findall(r"{{([A-Z_]+)}}", p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")))
                except UnicodeDecodeError:
                    pass
        say(f"  {kind}: placeholders {', '.join(sorted(found))}")
        unknown = found - {"NAME", "REPO", "URL", "OWNER", "YEAR", "TAGLINE", "MAIL"}
        if unknown:
            fail(f"{kind}: placeholders `site new` doesn't fill: {', '.join(sorted(unknown))}")
        for c in kinds[kind].get("collections") or []:
            if not (HERE / "templates" / "collections" / c / "collection.json").exists():
                fail(f"{kind}: template.json names a collection that doesn't exist: {c}")
    if not (SHELL_DIR / "functions" / "_lib" / "core.js").exists():
        fail(f"the data layer's shell is missing at {SHELL_DIR}")
    say(f"  client tool: {CLIENT_BIN if CLIENT_BIN.exists() else shutil.which('client') or 'MISSING'}")
    say("== cloudflare")
    tok, acct = cf_creds(required=False)
    if not (tok and acct):
        fail("CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN / CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID missing from the toolbelt (setenv.sh; TAYLOR-TODO §1)")
    else:
        try:
            projects = cf_api("GET", "/pages/projects") or []
            say(f"  token ok; {len(projects)} Pages project(s): {', '.join(p['name'] for p in projects) or '-'}")
        except SystemExit:
            fail("Cloudflare token or account id is refused (see the line above)")
        say(f"  wrangler: {'present' if WRANGLER.exists() else 'MISSING (claude-tools/install.sh)'}")
        say(f"  registry: {REGISTRY} ({sum(len(v) for v in registry_load().values())} site(s))")
        try:
            cf_api("GET", "/d1/database?per_page=1")
            say("  D1: the token can manage databases (site data / --db)")
        except SystemExit:
            say("  note: the token can't manage D1 yet, so `site data` / `--db` refuse "
                "(TAYLOR-TODO §1 \"Give the Cloudflare token D1\")")
    if (Path.cwd() / ".client.json").exists():
        ws, meta = workspace()
        say(f"== workspace {meta['slug']} ({meta['name']}) live_url={meta.get('live_url') or '-'}")
        for n in repos_of(ws):
            d = ws / "repos" / n
            slug = remote_slug(d)
            entry = site_entry(meta, n)
            if entry and entry.get("host") == "cloudflare":
                proj = entry["project"]
                p = cf_project(proj) if tok else None
                if not p:
                    fail(f"repos/{n}: registered as Pages project {proj} but Cloudflare has no such project")
                    continue
                dep = (p.get("latest_deployment") or {})
                url = f"https://{pages_host(proj)}/"
                cc = curl_header(url, "Cache-Control")
                say(f"  repos/{n}: {slug} -> {url} last publish {(dep.get('created_on') or '-')[:19]} "
                    f"Cache-Control: {cc or '-'}")
                off = badge_off(ws)
                (say if (has_badge(d) or off) else fail)(
                    f"  repos/{n}: badge " + ("in the repo, off on the site (badge: off in NOTES.md)" if off and has_badge(d)
                                              else "off (badge: off in NOTES.md)" if off
                                              else "\"Patched by Patchlamp\" in the footer"
                                              if has_badge(d) else
                                              "MISSING from index.html and NOTES.md has no `badge: off` (B60)"))
                ping = entry.get("indexnow") or {}
                say(f"  repos/{n}: IndexNow " + (f"{'accepted' if ping.get('ok') else 'refused'} "
                                                 f"{ping.get('urls')} URL(s) at {(ping.get('at') or '')[:19]}"
                                                 f" (status {ping.get('status')})" if ping else
                                                 "no ping recorded yet (the next site publish sends one)"))
                if entry.get("d1") or (d / "functions").is_dir():
                    problem = binding_problem(d, entry)
                    (fail if problem else say)(f"  repos/{n}: database " + (problem or f"{entry['d1']['name']} bound as DB (db doctor for the rest)"))
                    if (d / "functions" / "_lib" / "core.js").exists():
                        drift = shell_drift(d)
                        say(f"  repos/{n}: /admin shell " + (f"NOTE {len(drift)} file(s) behind the toolbelt (site shell {n})" if drift else "current"))
                vars_ = ((p.get("deployment_configs") or {}).get("production") or {}).get("env_vars") or {}
                if "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY" in vars_:
                    via = "connected (the owner's account on our platform key)" if "STRIPE_ACCOUNT" in vars_ else "key (the owner's own key, the fallback)"
                    hook = "STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET" in vars_
                    (say if hook else fail)(f"  repos/{n}: checkout {via}" + ("" if hook else
                        " but no STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, so no order is ever marked paid (site checkout again)"))
                elif (d / "functions" / "api" / "checkout.js").exists():
                    say(f"  repos/{n}: checkout off (site checkout {n} --connected once the owner's Stripe is connected)")
                if cc and "no-cache" not in cc and "max-age=0" not in cc:
                    fail(f"repos/{n}: HTML is cacheable (copy templates/sites/business/_headers into the repo root)")
                for dm in cf_domains(proj):
                    ok_ = dm.get("status") == "active"
                    (say if ok_ else fail)(f"  repos/{n}: domain {dm['name']} {dm.get('status')}"
                                           + ("" if ok_ else " (DNS records not pointing here yet?)"))
                continue
            info = pages_info(slug) if slug else None
            if not slug:
                fail(f"repos/{n}: no GitHub remote")
            elif not info:
                say(f"  repos/{n}: {slug}, Pages off or not visible")
            else:
                st = info.get("status") or "?"
                say(f"  repos/{n}: {slug} → {info.get('html_url')} [{st}]"
                    + (f" domain={info['cname']}" if info.get("cname") else ""))
                if st == "errored":
                    fail(f"repos/{n}: Pages build errored (gh run list -R {slug})")
    else:
        say("== not in a client workspace (cd ~/projects/clients/<slug> for per-repo checks)")
    watch_doctor(fail)
    mail_doctor(say, fail)
    if (Path.cwd() / ".client.json").exists():
        handover_doctor(say, fail)
    sys.exit(0 if ok else 1)


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="site", description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    n = sub.add_parser("new", help="create a site: repo from the template, Cloudflare Pages project, first publish, URL into the workspace")
    n.add_argument("name", help="repo name, e.g. <slug>-site")
    n.add_argument("--template", metavar="TYPE", help="the kind of site (site templates lists them; default business, "
                   "or the workspace's .client.json template)")
    n.add_argument("--tagline", help="one line under the name on the home page")
    n.add_argument("--primary", action="store_true", help="make this the workspace's live_url even if one is set")
    n.add_argument("--no-wait", action="store_true", help="don't wait for the first Pages build")
    n.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="check everything and print the plan; create nothing")
    n.add_argument("--gh-pages", action="store_true", help="serve from GitHub Pages instead of Cloudflare (legacy)")
    n.add_argument("--db", action="store_true", help="give it its own database and /admin (site data) before the first publish")
    n.add_argument("--owner", help="with --db: the email that signs in to /admin (default: the workspace's contact)")
    n.set_defaults(fn=cmd_new)
    sub.add_parser("templates", help="the kinds of site --template takes").set_defaults(fn=cmd_templates)
    ck = sub.add_parser("checkout", help="(SITE_ADMIN=1) switch a site's Stripe Checkout on: --connected (the path) or --key-from (fallback), or --off")
    ck.add_argument("name")
    ck.add_argument("--connected", action="store_true", help="the owner's Stripe connected to our platform (patchlamp.com's stripe row)")
    ck.add_argument("--test", action="store_true", help="with --connected: a test-mode account, on STRIPE_TEST_KEY")
    ck.add_argument("--key-from", metavar="NAME", help="fallback: toolbelt key holding the owner's own Stripe secret key")
    ck.add_argument("--webhook", action="store_true", help="also create the Stripe webhook that marks orders paid")
    ck.add_argument("--live", action="store_true", help="allow a live key (real money)")
    ck.add_argument("--off", action="store_true", help="remove the key, the account and the webhook secret")
    ck.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ck.set_defaults(fn=cmd_checkout)
    dt = sub.add_parser("data", help="give a site its own D1 database, /admin with an emailed sign-in, and the Functions shell")
    dt.add_argument("name", help="repo name under ./repos")
    dt.add_argument("--owner", help="the email that signs in to /admin (default: the workspace's contact)")
    dt.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    dt.set_defaults(fn=cmd_data)
    sh = sub.add_parser("shell", help="bring a site's /admin shell up to the toolbelt's, commit, push, publish (--check: only say)")
    sh.add_argument("name", nargs="?", help="repo name under ./repos (default: every site here with a database)")
    sh.add_argument("--check", action="store_true", help="say what's behind, change nothing (exit 1 when behind)")
    sh.add_argument("-m", "--message", help="the commit message")
    sh.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    sh.set_defaults(fn=cmd_shell)
    pb = sub.add_parser("publish", help="HEAD of ./repos/<name> -> its Cloudflare Pages project (commit + push first)")
    pb.add_argument("name", nargs="?", help="repo name under ./repos (optional when there is one)")
    pb.add_argument("--no-ping", action="store_true",
                    help="don't tell IndexNow what changed (B49; a ping never fails a publish anyway)")
    pb.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    pb.set_defaults(fn=cmd_publish)
    pv = sub.add_parser("previews", help=f"(SITE_ADMIN=1) publish a preview tree to the one {PREVIEWS_PROJECT} project (B45; `leads preview` drives it)")
    pv.add_argument("dir", nargs="?", default=".", help="the tree to upload (default .)")
    pv.add_argument("--project", help=f"Pages project (default {PREVIEWS_PROJECT})")
    pv.add_argument("--ls", action="store_true", help="the project, its host and its domains; upload nothing")
    pv.add_argument("--yes", action="store_true",
                    help="create the project on the first publish — Taylor's word, once (TAYLOR-TODO §1)")
    pv.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    pv.set_defaults(fn=cmd_previews)
    wt = sub.add_parser("watch", help="every live site and preview checked (B72): --once is one pass (site-watch.timer); alone, the last one")
    wt.add_argument("--once", action="store_true", help="check now, write sms-relay/state/uptime.json, tell Taylor what changed")
    wt.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="check and print; write nothing, tell nobody")
    wt.add_argument("--rdap", action="store_true", help="read custom domains' expiry now, not only once a week")
    wt.add_argument("--site", action="append", metavar="KEY", help="only this slug, <slug>/<repo> or preview/<slug> (repeatable)")
    wt.add_argument("--pretend-down", action="append", metavar="SITE",
                    help="TEST ONLY: treat this slug or key as failing, for a rehearsal of the down/up texts")
    wt.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="the record as JSON")
    wt.set_defaults(fn=cmd_watch)
    ad = sub.add_parser("adopt", help="register an existing repo as a Cloudflare site and create its project (SITE_ADMIN=1)")
    ad.add_argument("name"); ad.add_argument("--project", help="Pages project name (default: the repo name)")
    ad.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ad.set_defaults(fn=cmd_adopt)
    ml = sub.add_parser("mail", help="the site's address (B75): the mailbox on patchlamp.com + the Contact links; "
                        "`mail platform` / `mail doctor`")
    ml.add_argument("name", nargs="?", help="repo name under ./repos (default: every site here); or `platform` "
                    "(SITE_ADMIN=1: the Resend domain + Porkbun records) or `doctor`")
    ml.add_argument("--domain", metavar="D", help="(SITE_ADMIN=1) hello@D instead, for a zone on our Cloudflare account "
                    "whose apex has no MX")
    ml.add_argument("--check", action="store_true", help="say what's off, change nothing (exit 1 when it is)")
    ml.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print every write (Resend, DNS, the PUT, the commit); make none")
    ml.set_defaults(fn=cmd_mail)
    sub.add_parser("ls", help="repos in ./repos with their Pages URLs").set_defaults(fn=cmd_ls)
    st = sub.add_parser("stamp", help="(GitHub Pages sites only) new build id into version.json + every page's cache-buster")
    st.add_argument("name", help="repo name under ./repos")
    st.add_argument("--commit", metavar="MSG", help="git add -A && git commit -m MSG in that repo afterwards")
    st.set_defaults(fn=cmd_stamp)
    d = sub.add_parser("domain", help="custom domain for a site (SITE_ADMIN=1); no domain = show status")
    d.add_argument("name"); d.add_argument("domain", nargs="?")
    d.add_argument("--https", action="store_true", help="enforce HTTPS (works once GitHub has the certificate)")
    d.set_defaults(fn=cmd_domain)
    t = sub.add_parser("transfer", help="hand a repo to the client's GitHub account (SITE_ADMIN=1)")
    t.add_argument("name"); t.add_argument("user")
    t.add_argument("--keep", action="store_true", help="keep the local clone in repos/")
    t.set_defaults(fn=cmd_transfer)
    ho = sub.add_parser("handover", help="everything that is the client's -> handover/<date>/ + one zip for SEND-FILE, on their account page (B69)")
    ho.add_argument("name", nargs="?", help="one repo under ./repos (default: every site here)")
    ho.add_argument("--out", help="build here instead of handover/<date>/")
    ho.add_argument("--no-upload", action="store_true", help="don't put the zip on the account page")
    ho.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ho.set_defaults(fn=cmd_handover)
    rt = sub.add_parser("retire", help="take a site down: Pages project, registry row, local clone; the repo stays unless --delete-repo (SITE_ADMIN=1)")
    rt.add_argument("name")
    rt.add_argument("--delete-repo", action="store_true", help="also delete the GitHub repo (throwaway runs)")
    rt.add_argument("--keep-local", action="store_true", help="keep repos/<name> in the workspace")
    rt.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    rt.set_defaults(fn=cmd_retire)
    tp = sub.add_parser("template", help="`site template push` mirrors templates/sites/<T> to <org>/site-template(-<T>)")
    tp.add_argument("action", choices=["push"]); tp.add_argument("--template", metavar="TYPE")
    tp.set_defaults(fn=cmd_template)
    sub.add_parser("doctor", help="check auth, org, template, and this workspace's sites").set_defaults(fn=cmd_doctor)
    a = ap.parse_args()
    a.fn(a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
